@@section 1
@@title SQ-PWG Power Grid performance measuring, 2026-11-12 ([power_grid.md](../power_grid.md) 5.4 H5, D14; [energy_advanced.md](../energy_advanced.md) 7; TODO `largecontent/mod-additions #74`)
@@date 2026-11-12
@@jars powergrid
@@sources feature_writeup/power_grid.md feature_writeup/energy_advanced.md
@@text
@@text **Refreshed 2026-11-13 for the P2 build** (was held until a port existed): jar `jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-03.jar` (port phase 2: creative
@@text sources, creative resistors, gauges, wires; enough for the D14 measurement). Defines how the server cost and the client
@@text mirror cost are measured so D14 (keep the client mirror or go server-values-only) can be decided from numbers. Use a perf
@@text session as the queue header says (JFR on, rows marked), a fresh superflat world, the jar copied into `OUT/srv/mods/` only
@@text (never `mods/`), and `tools/scratch_query/pwg_grid_probe.js` copied to `OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_pwg_grid_probe.js`.
@@text Grids are built by the probe (`zpwgg ladder X Y Z N`: N creative resistors of 1 k in series, about 2N solver nodes, rows of
@@text 20, source 100 V; `zpwgg grids X Y Z COUNT N`), so every run has the same shape. `forceload add` the area first (a ladder
@@text of N spans 40 x (3 x N / 20) blocks south of X Y Z; grids add 50 blocks east per grid). Solver counters:
@@text `powergrid performance get NetSolve`, `... get JavaMNA`, `... get minecraft:overworld` (console; min / max / avg in
@@text microseconds). The native solver is not ported (D4), so all rows are the Java backend. The client-mirror switch is
@@text `clientMirror` in `OUT/srv/config/powergrid-common.toml` (read on the server: false stops the per-tick state stream;
@@text clients then see the full sync every `fullStateSynchronizationInterval` ticks, default 100). Coordinates below: X 1000,
@@text Y -60 (superflat grass at -61), Z 1000.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-PWG-01 | baseline: no grid, 5 min idle (perf segment)
@group A
@commands no grid; `forceload add 992 992 1100 1100`; 5 min idle; `perf_session.sh mark SQ-PWG-01`; `powergrid performance get minecraft:overworld`
@pass baseline mean and p99 tick recorded; counter prints (near 0 us)
@fails n/a
@from batches/r1113pwg/pwgperf.qb
> forceload add 992 992 1100 1100
> gamerule doMobSpawning false
> weather clear
sleep 30
> forge tps
sleep 300
> forge tps
> powergrid performance get minecraft:overworld
sleep 3
reject An unexpected error occurred
look record mean / p99 tick of this segment from the perf session (baseline for -02 to -07); counter near 0 us or "no measurement"

## SQ-PWG-02 | ladder 25 (about 50 nodes), 5 min
@group A
@commands `zpwgg ladder 1000 -60 1000 25` (about 50 nodes); wait 200 ticks; 5 min; `powergrid performance get NetSolve`, `... JavaMNA`, `... minecraft:overworld`; `zpwgg net 1002 -60 1000`
@pass `[zpwgg] ladder built n=25`; mean tick delta against SQ-PWG-01 under 0.1 ms; `net paused=false` and networkNodes about 50; no `Converged after` stdout spam (the solver logger is wired in P2)
@fails solver hooks, matrix reuse; a paused net: chunk not ticking (forceload)
@from batches/r1113pwg/pwgperf.qb
