## SQ-PWG-27 | FE inverter: fill 20000 FE, measure N6 (FE per tick per watt) three times
@group A
@commands PWG-18 and N6, Z 1020: `zpwg3 place 1103 -60 1020 powergrid:fe_inverter facing=down`; `zpwg3 place 1106 -60 1020 powergrid:current_gauge`; `zpwg3 place 1109 -60 1020 powergrid:creative_resistor`; `zpwg3 res 1109 -60 1020 45` (100 ohm); `zpwg3 place 1109 -60 1022 powergrid:voltage_gauge`; wires: inverter T0 to gauge T0, gauge T1 to resistor T0, resistor T1 to inverter T1, resistor T0 and T1 to the voltage gauge T0 and T1 (control terminal T2 left open); `zpwg3 fe 1103 -60 1020 down 20000`; at once `zpwg3 be 1106 -60 1020` and `zpwg3 be 1109 -60 1022`; wait 10 ticks; `zpwg3 feget 1103 -60 1020 down`; `be` both gauges again; repeat the fill and the 10-tick window twice more
@pass `fe received 20000`; each window: N6 = (20000 - stored after) / (t after - t of the fill) / P, with P the mean of I x V over the two gauge reads (watts at the load); record the three N6 values: the port keeps upstream's rate, so N6 is about 10 (FE per tick per watt; `ceil` rounding adds up to 1 FE per tick); output voltage near `stored / 2` volts (2 FE per V) times I / I(no throttle); no ERROR
