@@text
@@text **P4 update 2026-11-13 (kinetics: motors, generator set, rheostat, variac, servo):** jar
@@text `jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-05.jar` (sha1 d1f81955619dc734045bf2b0774c820daabf7b3d; port phase 4) supersedes `-04` for every row
@@text from here on (P2 and P3 rows still pass on it; rerun only those their runs flag). It adds 13 blocks (Electric Motor,
@@text Constant Speed Motor, servo, rheostat, variac, conductive casing, generator clutch, induction rotor, large induction rotor,
@@text horizontal and vertical commutator, horizontal and vertical generator housing) with their items, 9 block entity types,
@@text 25 recipes (47 in all), the clutch display source, generator speeds in the stress provider, and the mixin
@@text `KineticBlockEntityAccessor` (16 in all). P2 to P4 are D1's "phase 1", the first evaluation point. Probe
@@text `tools/scratch_query/pwg_p4_probe.js` copied to `OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_pwg_p4_probe.js` (commands in its
@@text header) next to the three earlier probes. Superflat; motors at Y -60 (floor -61), generator lines at Y -58 so windings
@@text fit above and below. `forceload add 1090 1140 1140 1260` before any build. Terminal numbers: `zpwg3 be` or `zpwg4 kin`
@@text list `T0=...` per terminal (creative source T0 is the positive side). Numbers below assume the default
@@text `powergrid-server.toml` (stress impacts, `torqueForStress` 15, `windingCoilConstant` 5, `fieldSaturationCurrent` 2,
@@text `motorDynamicResistance` true, `motorMinimumLoad` 0.05); Create's own impacts are read from the game (`impact=` in
@@text `zpwg4 kin`), never assumed. Notes: `development/backportedPowerGrid/PORT_NOTES.md` section 14.
@@text
@@text Formulas used in the pass lines: Electric Motor speed = 0.003835 x Vm^2 RPM (Vm = motor terminal voltage; capped at
@@text 256, truncated to an integer), motor current = Vm / (25.6 / load) with load = Create stress / capacity clamped to
@@text 0.05..1; winding field f(I) = 5 x (2 tanh(0.75 I) + 0.05 I) + 0.001 per winding; an induction rotor's field is the sum of
@@text the windings on its 4 sides / 4; a commutator's EMF = (sum of its rotors' fields) x RPM x pi / 30; clutch stress = (sum
@@text of the assembly's impacts: clutch 32, induction rotor 32, large 128, commutator 8) x (15 - redstone) / 15 per RPM.
@@text
@@text **Run order (high priority first):** SQ-PWG-35 (boot, registry, mixin, stress provider), CQ-PWG-13 (client boot,
@@text renderers, connected textures), SQ-PWG-36 (recipes, configs), SQ-PWG-37 (PWG-06 motor speed, `KineticBlockEntityAccessor`
@@text under flicker), SQ-PWG-38 (PWG-07 and PWG-08: motor driving a Create network and a generator fed by Create rotation,
@@text with numbers), SQ-PWG-39 (PWG-10 generator load), SQ-PWG-40 (`spinning_rotor` damage); then SQ-PWG-41 (clutch motor
@@text mode), -42 (PWG-09 self-excited), -43 (rheostat, variac, servo, fix B9), -44 (PWG-11 carbon pile); SQ-PWG-07 last (perf
