@group A
@commands PWG-11 on SQ-PWG-38 B at 256 RPM (Z 1180): unregulated first: `zpwg3 res 1110 -60 1180 45` (100 ohm), wait 60, `zpwg3 be 1110 -60 1182`; `zpwg3 res 1110 -60 1180 36` (10 ohm), wait 60, `be` again. Regulator: `zpwg3 place 1097 -60 1186 powergrid:carbon_pile_coil`; `zpwg3 place 1097 -59 1186 minecraft:coal_block` (turns into a carbon pile; if not, `zpwg3 place 1097 -59 1186 powergrid:carbon_pile`); move the excitation loop through the pile: `setblock 1098 -58 1183 minecraft:air`, `zpwg3 src 1098 -58 1183 60`, wires source T0 to coil T2, coil T3 to connector 1101 -57 1180 T0, connector 1101 -59 1180 T1 to source T1 (the connector-to-connector wire stays); sense: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1186 powergrid:creative_resistor`, `res ... 54` (1 k), wires commutator 1104 -58 1180 T0 to that resistor T0, its T1 to coil T0, coil T1 to commutator T1; `zpwg3 res 1110 -60 1180 45`, wait 100, `be 1110 -60 1182`, `zpwg3 be 1097 -60 1186`; `zpwg3 res 1110 -60 1180 36`, wait 100, the same reads
@pass record the load voltage at 100 and 10 ohm without and with the regulator; the change between the two loads is smaller with the regulator (PWG-11: within a few volts; record the two differences and the pile resistance from the coil's goggle lines); no ERROR
@fails `CarbonPileCoilBlockEntity` (`coilPull` saturates at 0.4 A coil current, pile resistance base x trim x (1 + pull^1.5 x gain)); a regulator that does nothing: the sense resistor (lower it to 300 ohm, index 47) or the trim (`zpwg3 scroll 1097 -59 1186`)
