## SQ-PWG-07 | generator set at 256 RPM with a 10 ohm load and the motor line: 5 min, rotor steadiness, load steps
@group A
@commands perf session row (needs SQ-PWG-01's baseline; moved here from the performance section, now runnable): fresh superflat, `forceload add 1090 1140 1140 1260`; build SQ-PWG-38 B at 256 RPM with the 10 ohm load and SQ-PWG-38 A with 4 presses; wait 200 ticks; `perf_session.sh mark SQ-PWG-07`; 5 min; `powergrid performance get NetSolve`, `... get JavaMNA`, `... get minecraft:overworld`; during the 5 min `zpwg4 kin 1102 -58 1180` 10 times 20 ticks apart; then `zpwg3 res 1110 -60 1180 27` and back to 36 every 10 s for 1 min (load steps) with `kin 1102 -58 1180` after each
@pass mean tick delta against SQ-PWG-01 under 0.2 ms (record; the generator adds non-linear coupling and per-tick force exchange); rotor `rpm=` steady: the 10 samples within 2 % of each other (PD gains `rotorKp` 0.85, `rotorKd` 0.002 do not oscillate on Create 0.5.1's tick); after each load step the rotor settles within 60 ticks without overshooting past 272 RPM (`rotorRPMMax`; no rotor destroyed); no `did not converge` / convergence problem lines and no `Converged after` spam
@fails `GeneratorCoupling` (back-EMF residual, `postUpperSolve` force), `RotorBehaviour.tick` (PD), solver iterations (`CSolver` limits)
