## CQ-PWG-14
@group client
@commands PWG-32. Client boot with the `-06` jar (client mods plus the jar; never `mods/` of the instance), single-player superflat world with cheats (`sp_world.py`), creative; then by chat (`qrun.py client`, xdotool) for each component below: `/create ponder <component>`, wait 3 s, screenshot `RES/shots/CQ-PWG-14_<scene>_a.png`, wait the scene length + 5 s, screenshot `..._b.png`; for components with several scenes press `d` (next scene) and repeat; `Esc` before the next command. Components and their scenes in order (seconds): `powergrid:voltage_gauge` voltage_gauge (27); `powergrid:energy_meter` energy_meter (33); `powergrid:copper_coil` generator_winding (8), parallel_generator_winding (12), generator_1 (37), generator_2 (53); `powergrid:generator_clutch` generator_clutch (15); `powergrid:generator_housing` generator_housing (11); `powergrid:generator_induction_rotor` generator_rotor (11); `powergrid:insulated_copper_wire` insulated_wire (7), wire_voltage_drop (18); `powergrid:wire_connector` wire_connector (10); `powergrid:grounding_rod` grounding (13), improved_grounding (13); `powergrid:cord_junction` cord_junction (6); `powergrid:socket` cord_socket (6); `powergrid:transformer_core` transformer_sizes (11), transformer_winding (27), transformer_nether (15); `powergrid:variac` variac (8); `powergrid:rheostat` rheostat (8); `powergrid:power_resistor` power_resistor (14); `powergrid:carbon_pile_coil` carbon_pile (26); `powergrid:device_connector` device_connector (14); `powergrid:hv_switch` hv_switch (6); `powergrid:redstone_converter` redstone_converter (33); `powergrid:contactor` contactor (7), contactor_stack (9); `powergrid:fuse_holder` fuse (14); `powergrid:electric_motor` electric_motor (11); `powergrid:constant_speed_motor` constant_speed_motor (14); `powergrid:servo` servo (11); `powergrid:electromagnet` electromagnet (19); `powergrid:battery` battery (12); `powergrid:magnet` thunder_magnet (7), lightning_attractor (10); `minecraft:lightning_rod` lightning_attractor (10). Then `/create ponder` (index; screenshot), click each of the three Power Grid tags (screenshot). 36 scenes, about 12 min
@pass client reaches a world; every command opens its ponder (no `Could not find` / no ponder chat error); 72 scene screenshots plus index and 3 tag pages; LOOK per scene: title and text in English (no raw `powergrid.ponder.` key, no `unregistered`), no missing block in the structure (no gap or air where a block belongs, no purple/black model), wires appear (hanging and cord), gauges and meters show values after the source turns on, kinetic parts turn where the text says so; `_b` shows the end of the scene (last text shown, the timeline at the end); the index shows the three tags with their icons (induction rotor, MV switch, Electric Motor); the tag pages list their P2 to P4 members; `logs/latest.log` of the client: no `Failed to read ponder schematic`, no exception with `org.patryk3211.powergrid` or `foundation.ponder` in its stack, no `Error occurred`
@fails scene does not open: registration (`PowerGridPonderScenes`, `PowerGridClientImpl.clientSetup` ran: search the log for the ponder ids); raw keys: lang file shipped whole (`assets/powergrid/lang/en_us.json`), text numbering (`PonderScene.registerText`); missing blocks: SQ-PWG-45 result for that file; a circuit that never comes alive (gauges at 0): the restore hook (`PowerGridPonderPlugin.onPonderLevelRestore`, first instruction of each scene) or `ElectricityTickInstruction`; stack in `WireElement.renderLast`: the wire entity factory on a `PonderWorld`
