## SQ-PWG-49 | PWG-21 basin heater: FD cooking pot heat levels, skillet cooks, basin heated mixing (FLR-05 build order: mixer, then motor at 64 by NBT) and its 0 V control
@group A
@commands PWG-21 and the Farmer's Delight mixins, Z 1420 to 1430. Pot: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1420 powergrid:basin_heater`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1423 0`; wires source T0 to heater T0, heater T1 to source T1; `zpwg3 place 1100 -59 1420 farmersdelight:cooking_pot`; `zpwg6 heater 1100 -60 1420`, `zpwg6 fd 1100 -59 1420`; then the source at 140, 200 and 250 V (`zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1423 V`), wait 100 ticks after each, both reads again. Skillet: `zpwg3 place 1103 -60 1420 powergrid:basin_heater`, `zpwg3 src 1103 -60 1423 200` wired the same, `zpwg3 place 1103 -59 1420 farmersdelight:skillet`; wait 100; `zpwg6 skillet 1103 -59 1420 minecraft:beef`; `zpwg6 fd 1103 -59 1420` now and every 100 ticks for 800 ticks; `zpwg3 count 1103 -59 1420 2 minecraft:cooked_beef`. Basin: `zpwg3 place 1106 -60 1420 powergrid:basin_heater`, `zpwg3 src 1106 -60 1423 200` wired, `zpwg3 place 1106 -59 1420 create:basin`; in the FLR-05 rig's order (r1113 pwg10: a mixer placed under a running motor never joined its network) the mixer first, `setblock 1106 -57 1420 create:mechanical_mixer`, then `setblock 1106 -56 1420 create:creative_motor[facing=down]{ScrollValue:64}`; wait 40; `zpwg4 kin 1106 -57 1420` (mixer; speed 64 before anything else, else stop: the basin part is void); `zpwg4 kin 1106 -56 1420` (motor), `zpwg4 kin 1106 -57 1420` (mixer); `zpwg6 heater 1106 -60 1420`; `zpwg6 insert 1106 -59 1420 minecraft:copper_ingot 1`; `zpwg6 insert 1106 -59 1420 create:zinc_ingot 1`; `cdevtest inv 1106 -59 1420` every 40 ticks for 400 ticks, `zpwg4 kin 1106 -57 1420`; then `zpwg3 src 1106 -60 1423 0`, wait 100, insert copper and zinc again, `inv` every 40 ticks for 400 ticks
@pass pot: at 0 V `heat_level=NONE`, `isHeated=false`; at 140 V `heat_level=FADING` (about 400 C), `isHeated=true fdHeatSourceOnly=false` (the HEAD inject: heat level at least fading counts, as upstream); at 200 V `KINDLED` (about 800 C, block light 12, `boilerHeat=1`, `basinSees=KINDLED`); at 250 V `SEETHING` (about 1250 C, light 15, `boilerHeat=2`, `basinSees=SEETHING`: superheated recipes would run); skillet: `isCooking=true isHeated=false` while the beef is on it (the redirect in `isCooking`; no FD heat source below), and the beef turns into `minecraft:cooked_beef` (on the skillet or as a dropped item) within 800 ticks (the `cookingTick` redirect); basin: the motor and the mixer at speed 64 (`kin`), brass (`create:brass_ingot x2`) from copper and zinc at 200 V (heated mixing), none at 0 V; no ERROR
@fails `isHeated` false over a kindled heater: `CookingPotBlockEntityMixin` did not apply or another mod changed `isHeated` (Create Central Kitchen injects `processCooking` only); skillet never cooks: `SkilletBlockEntityMixin` `cookingTick` redirect; heat level stays none: `BasinHeaterBlockEntity.electricalTick` or the wiring; boiler heat -1: `BoilerHeaters.registerHeater` (`ModdedBlocks.BASIN_HEATER` `onRegister`); basin sees none: `BasinBlockEntity.getHeatLevelOf` reads `blaze` (Create's `HEAT_LEVEL`)
