## SQ-PWG-51 | PWG-33 electric pump: tank to tank, the pipe placed after the pump starts is picked up (FluidPropagatorMixin); fill diagnostics
@group A
@commands PWG-33 pump and `FluidPropagatorMixin`, Z 1450. `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1450 create:fluid_tank`; `zpwg3 place 1104 -60 1450 create:fluid_tank`; wait 40; `zpwg6 fill 1100 -60 1450 minecraft:water 8000` (the probe builds the FluidStack from NBT: `new FluidStack(fluid, mb)` is ambiguous in Rhino; it prints `fill stack ... amount= handler= tanks= isFluidValid=`, and when the capability takes 0 mB, as on r1113 pwg10, it fills the tank's inventory, the controller's, and names the route `via ...`), `cdevtest tank 1100 -60 1450`; `zpwg3 place 1101 -60 1450 create:fluid_pipe`; `zpwg3 place 1102 -60 1450 powergrid:electric_pump facing=east`; `zpwg3 src 1102 -60 1453 120` wired to the pump; wait 40; `zpwg6 pump 1102 -60 1450`; then place the last pipe after the pump runs: `zpwg3 place 1103 -60 1450 create:fluid_pipe`; `cdevtest tank 1104 -60 1450` every 40 ticks (tank lines carry no position: 1100 is read only before and at the end) for 200 ticks; `zpwg3 src 1102 -60 1453 240`, wait 40, `pump`, `tank` twice 40 ticks apart; `zpwg3 src 1102 -60 1453 0`, wait 40, `pump`, `tank` twice 40 ticks apart
@pass `fill minecraft:water 8000 via ...` (record the route and the `fill stack` line); `pump` speed non-zero at 120 V and higher at 240 V (record both; 480 ohm, `electricPumpPower` 2.135), 0 at 0 V; water moves from the first tank to the second after the last pipe is placed (the pipe placed after the pump started is picked up: `FluidPropagatorMixin` calls `updatePipesOnSide`); the rate rises with the voltage; no flow at 0 V; no ERROR
@fails `fill ... 0` on every route: a probe fault (record the `fill stack` line), not Power Grid; no flow at all: pump facing (try `facing=west`) or pipe connections (re-place a pipe); flow only when the pump is re-placed after the pipes: `FluidPropagatorMixin` (`propagateChangedPipe`, `@Local` ordinal of `target`); speed 0: wiring
