## SQ-PWG-52 | PWG-33 lights: fixture power and own emission by voltage, LV bulb power 1 then burns out at 120 V, factory light power 3 lights 15 down
@group A
@commands PWG-33 lights, Z 1460 to 1470 (Y -60 ground). Fixture: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1460 powergrid:light_fixture`; `zpwg6 bulb 1100 -60 1460 powergrid:light_bulb`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1463 120` wired to the fixture; `zpwg6 light 1100 -60 1460` every 20 ticks for 120 ticks; then 60 V, wait 200, `light`; then 0 V, wait 200, `light`. LV bulb: `zpwg3 place 1103 -60 1460 powergrid:light_fixture`, `zpwg6 bulb 1103 -60 1460 powergrid:lv_light_bulb`, `zpwg3 src 1103 -60 1463 12` wired; wait 200, `light`; then `zpwg3 src 1103 -60 1463 120`, `light` every 10 ticks for 60 ticks; `zpwgg overheated 1103 -60 1460 1`. Factory light 17 blocks up: `zpwg3 place 1106 -43 1466 powergrid:factory_light`; `zpwg6 bulb 1106 -43 1466 powergrid:light_bulb`; `zpwg3 src 1106 -60 1468 120`, wires from the source to the factory light's T0 and T1 (long hanging wires; `powergrid:wire` reaches 16 blocks: put a `powergrid:wire_connector` on a pillar if it does not); wait 200; `zpwg6 light 1106 -43 1466`
@pass fixture at 120 V: `power=2` within 120 ticks, `T=` about 1450, `emission=15` (the fixture's own block-state light; `blockLight` also counts the LV fixture 3 blocks east); at 60 V `power` 0 or 1 and a lower `emission` (record); at 0 V `power=0`, `emission=0`; LV bulb at 12 V `power=1`, `emission=10` (`LvLightBulb` caps the level at 1); at 120 V `burned=true` within 60 ticks and `power=0` (the bulb burns out; the fixture stays, no Overheated Component: `zpwgg` reports none); factory light: state `power=3` (bulb level 2 + 1), `emission=15`, `factory light blocks below=15 deepest=15` (`projectDown` loops 1 to range - 1, range 16: upstream loop) and `blockLight16` above 0; no ERROR
@fails no bulb: `bulb` reports none (the saved-data route: `AbstractLightFixtureBlockEntity.read`); power stays 0 at 120 V: filament wiring or `LightBulbState.tick` (filament not converged); light level 0 with `power=2`: the block's `lightLevel` (`LightFixtureBlock` / `FactoryLightBlock`); no light blocks below a factory light: `FactoryLightBlockEntity.projectDown`, or the `factory_light_light` material (port: replaceable, destroyed on push, PORT_NOTES.md 16)
