## SQ-PWG-54 | rerun at X 1340 (pwgr1: p6 entityLine getUUID not found, fixed): rerun at X 1300 (pwg12 built it at X 1100): PWG-23 solar panel at noon, 4-panel series multiblock at 30 ohm, biome overrides (fix B10), night, solar panel bearing (lastException, contraptions all after assemble and 100 ticks later)
@group A
@commands PWG-23 and the `solar_biome_override` listener, Z 1500 to 1515. `time set 6000`; `weather clear`; panel A: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1500 powergrid:solar_panel facing=down`; `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1503 powergrid:creative_resistor`; `zpwg3 res 1100 -60 1503 33` (7 ohm, near the maximum power point); wires panel T0 to resistor T0, resistor T1 to panel T1; wait 100; `zpwg6 solar 1100 -60 1500` 3 times 20 ticks apart. Multiblock: `zpwg3 place 1101 -60 1500 powergrid:solar_panel facing=down`, the same at 1102 and 1103; `zpwg6 solarjoin 1100 -60 1500 1101 -60 1500`, then with 1102 and 1103; `zpwg3 res 1100 -60 1503 38` (30 ohm: `SolarPanelBlockEntity` builds the multiblock as a series string, `IVCurve(..., panelCount, 1)`, so its maximum power point is about 4 x 7 = 28 ohm, not 7/4 (r1113 pwg10); index i gives (i % 9 + 1) x 10^(i / 9 - 3)); wait 100; `solar 1100 -60 1500`. Override (desert temperature on plains; the superflat world has one biome): write `OUT/srv/<level-name>/datapacks/pwgsolar/pack.mcmeta` (`{"pack":{"pack_format":10,"description":"PWG solar overrides, scratch only"}}`) and two files in `OUT/srv/<level-name>/datapacks/pwgsolar/data/pwgsolar/powergrid/solar_biome_override/`: `plains_hot.json` = `{"biome":"minecraft:plains","overrideTemp":true,"biomeTemp":34.4,"overrideSolarConstant":false,"solarConstant":1361,"enableFullRotation":false,"disableWeather":false,"disableAtmosphere":false}` and `zz_swamp.json` = the same with `"biome":"minecraft:swamp"`; `/reload`; `datapack list enabled`; `zpwg6 check`; panel B: `zpwg3 place 1110 -60 1500 powergrid:solar_panel facing=down` with its own 7 ohm resistor at 1110 -60 1503 wired the same; wait 100; `solar 1110 -60 1500` 3 times; `solar 1100 -60 1500` once more. Night: `time set 18000`, wait 40, `solar 1110 -60 1500`. Bearing, Z 1510: `time set 6000`; `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1510 powergrid:solar_panel_bearing facing=up`; `zpwg3 place 1100 -59 1510 powergrid:solar_panel facing=down`; `zpwg3 place 1101 -59 1510 powergrid:solar_panel facing=down`; `zpwg6 solarjoin 1100 -59 1510 1101 -59 1510`; `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1513 powergrid:creative_resistor`, `res ... 33`, wired to the bearing's T0 and T1; `zpwg6 assemble 1100 -60 1510` (prints `assemble lastException=` from `getLastAssemblyException`, `running=`, the block above) and right after it `zpwg6 contraptions all 1100 -60 1510` (level-wide scan of `create:controlled_contraption` entities: id, position, removed, alive, Type, blocks, saved controller; and the bearing's `movedContraption`: null, set to a listed entity or set to one not in the level); wait 100; `zpwg6 contraptions all 1100 -60 1510` again; `zpwg6 contraption 1100 -59 1510 16` (radius 16, with a count per entity type in the box); `zpwg6 solar 1100 -60 1510` twice 200 ticks apart
@pass panel A at noon: terminals about 18 to 21 V across 7 ohm (record P = V^2 / 7; rated about 64 W at the maximum power point), `override=none`, sky 15; multiblock across 30 ohm: the goggle lines show 4 panels, current near one panel's (about 3.5 A), voltage about 4 x, P = V^2 / 30 about 3.5 to 4 times panel A's 7 ohm power (record); after `/reload`: log `Loaded 2 solar biome overrides`, `check` `solar biome overrides 2`; panel B: `override=constant=1361.0/false temp=34.4/true` (the plains file applies even with a second file: fix B10, upstream kept only the last file's match) and lower power than panel A's first reads (hotter cells: PWG-23 "desert lower"; record both); panel A unchanged (it read its biome entry at its first tick; upstream-same, datapack registries never change mid-world on 1.20.1); night: power 0; bearing: `assemble lastException=none running=true`, both `contraptions all` reads list one `controlled ... removed=false ... type=powergrid:solar_panel blocks=2 controller=1100,-60,1510 attachedToBearing=true` and `bearing ... movedContraption=set` (r1113 pwg10: `contraptions 0` 100 ticks after a successful assemble), `contraption create:controlled_contraption type=powergrid:solar_panel blocks=2`, the bearing's output non-zero at noon (record; it turns toward the sun: record the second read); no ERROR
@fails `Loaded 0`: the datapack path (`data/<ns>/powergrid/solar_biome_override/*.json`) or the listener (`PowerGridImpl.addReloadListeners`); override `none` on B: biome id (`level.getBiome` key `minecraft:plains`); no power at noon: panel facing (`facing=down` points the cells up), `skyVisible` (nothing above), resistor wiring; `solarjoin` fails: controller missing (`SolarPanelBlockEntity.getController`); no contraption: the `lastException` text; `running=true` but no entity: the two `contraptions all` reads tell apart an entity that never joined (`controlled=0` right after assemble, `movedContraption=set (entity not in the level)`: `addFreshEntity` refused) and one that discarded itself (listed right after assemble, gone or `removed=true` 100 ticks later: Create's `tickContraption` / the controller check in `ControlledContraptionEntity`); `none` with `running=false`: `SolarPanelBearingContraption.assemble` returned false (needs panels on the bearing's face) or the contraption type (SQ-PWG-46 `check`)
