@@text **P7 update 2026-11-13 (equipment):** jar `jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-09.jar`
@@text (sha1 5008eaaf00388d0982cfefe3330a36995e2fc730; port phase 7) supersedes `-08` for every row from here on (the P3 to P6
@@text rows stay valid on it: nothing of theirs changed except the `growthLampChance` config comment, B11). It adds the portable
@@text battery block (and its block entity), 6 items (portable battery, its placeable twin, portable drill, portable saw,
@@text Electro-Baton, Electro-Zapper), the zap projectile entity, 5 recipes, 3 mixins (`SheepMixin`, `forge.PlayerDrillMixin`,
@@text new `forge.DrillBreakActionMixin` on `ServerPlayerGameMode.handleBlockBreakAction`, which replaces upstream's 1.20 Forge
@@text left-click event; all `defaultRequire 1`), 4 packets, the lightning rod movement behavior (lightning attractor,
@@text registered in the common setup) and the battery armor layer and zapper render handler on the client. No new ponder scene
@@text (upstream has none for the equipment; the `lightning_attractor` scene shipped in P5). New probe
@@text `tools/scratch_query/pwg_p7_probe.js` (`zz_pwg_p7_probe.js`, `zpwg7`, commands in its header): one Forge fake player
@@text `[zpwg7]` uses the tools. A fake player never ticks, so the worn-battery tick and the drill's speed decay are called or
@@text read directly by the probe and their live hooks are checked in CQ-PWG-18. Area: X 1095 to 1115, Z 1525 to 1590, Y -60
@@text (`forceload add 1095 1525 1115 1590`). Battery numbers (defaults): 20 000 FE base, +20 000 per Capacity level; output
@@text fraction 1.0 at half charge or more, else charge fraction / 0.5, never under 0.25 (0 when the charge is below one use; the probe's `bat` asks for 1 FE);
@@text drill 25 FE per block, saw 100, baton 250 per hit, zapper 500 per shot. Damage rows hit villagers (the group A server
@@text discards animals; scratch-test gotchas); if a hit does nothing, Loading Protection may be canceling it (set
@@text `protectionDuration 1` as in r1112).
