## CQ-PWG-17
@group client
@commands P7 client boot with the `-09` jar (client mods plus the jar; never `mods/` of the instance), single-player superflat world with cheats, creative then survival: creative tab (Portable Battery, Portable Drill, Portable Saw, Electro-Baton, Electro-Zapper; no "placeable" entry); `/give @s powergrid:portable_battery{Charge:20000}`; `/enchant`-free check: hover the battery (tooltip: resistance, max power, current charge `100%`); put it on (chest slot), F5 front and back (screenshot `RES/shots/CQ-PWG-17_worn.png`); `/summon minecraft:armor_stand ~2 ~ ~` and put a battery on it; in survival hold each tool (first person and F5, screenshots); hold the drill and mine stone continuously for 5 s, release 5 s; shoot the zapper at a block and at a group of three villagers (`/summon minecraft:villager ~ ~ ~5 {NoAI:1b}` x3 close together); right-click the ground with the battery item (places the block); right-click the placed battery with an empty hand and an empty chest slot; F3 + H on, hover tools with the battery worn
@pass client reaches a world; no `Mixin apply failed`; LOOK: every P7 item has its model (no purple/black): drill with its head, saw, baton, zapper with its cog, battery; the worn battery is drawn on the back (battery armor layer; also on the armor stand) over the zinc chest armor texture; drill and saw use their own first-person pose (hand render hooks) and the drill head spins, faster while mining (server speed packet) and slowing after release; the zapper is held in the crossbow pose, recoils and plays its shot sound, its cog spins; the bolt renders (`entity/zap_projectile` texture) with spark particles; at the villagers zap arcs join the target to its neighbors with sparks along the arcs (fix B13: upstream scattered them off the line); a block hit throws sparks; the placed block shows the battery model; the empty-hand right-click puts it back in the chest slot with its charge; tool durability bars show the battery's charge bar (cream color) while the worn battery can power them; no `Error`, `Exception` or `Missing model` naming `powergrid` in the client log
@fails missing model: shipped `models/item/<id>.json` and `item/drill/head`, `item/electrozapper/cog` (`ModdedPartialModels`); no back layer: `PowerGridClientImpl.addEntityLayers`; no hand pose: `ForgeClientEvents.renderPlayerHand`; zapper silent or not recoiling: `ElectroZapperS2CPacket` (encoded with `ShootGadgetPacket.write`) and `PowerGridClient.ELECTRO_ZAPPER_RENDER_HANDLER.registerListeners`
