## CQ-PWG-18
@group client
@commands PWG-34 to -36 by hand, on a dedicated server (the `-09` jar on both sides; `protectionDuration 1` in the server's Loading Protection config): survival; `/give @s powergrid:portable_battery{Charge:20000}`, wear it; hold an item with Forge Energy (SQ-PWG-57 `feitems`) for 10 s and watch its bar; a 5 x 5 stone wall: hold the drill and mine it block by block without releasing (record the time for the first and the fifth block), release for 5 s, mine one more; fell a tree with the saw while sneaking; `/summon minecraft:zombie` (night) and hit it with the baton; shoot three grouped zombies with the zapper; keep using the drill until the battery passes 10 % and then empties (`/give` a battery with `{Charge:2100}` to get there fast)
@pass the held FE item fills while the battery charge falls (worn tick on the player tick); drilling speeds up over the first blocks (fifth block clearly faster than the first) and is back to the slow start after 5 s released (speed decays one step per tick, 80 ticks); the saw fells the tree; the baton slows the zombie to a stop for 3 s; the zapper bolt hurts and arcs between the zombies; at 10 % a title subtitle `Portable battery low` (gold) with a fail sound, at 25 FE `Portable battery empty` (red); then the drill keeps working at hand speed and wears its durability; no exception in either log
@fails no FE transfer: `PowerGrid.playerPre` (architectury `TickEvent.PLAYER_PRE`); no speed-up: the `start` / `stop` actions reach the server (`DrillBreakActionMixin`), `DrillSpeedS2CPacket`; no warning: `BatteryUtils.sendWarning` (title packets; lang keys `powergrid.gui.portable.battery.low` / `.depleted` ship)
