## SQ-PWG-63 | rerun with the p8 direct use (fake-player clicks no longer go through Create's value box handler): PWG-38 modular display: insert, flip coils, module type, dye and wrench on the slot, value box, removal, burnout, drops
@group A
@commands PWG-38 (modular display), Z 1600. `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1600 powergrid:modular_display facing=north`; `zpwg8 fp 1100 -60 1598`; `zpwg8 hold powergrid:display_module 4`; `zpwg8 use 1100 -60 1600 north 0.25 0.75 0.0` (slot 0); `zpwg8 use 1100 -60 1600 north 0.75 0.75 0.0` (slot 1); `zpwg8 md 1100 -60 1600`. Coils (slot 0: positive T0, reset T1, case common T8): `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1603 0`; `zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1603 0 1100 -60 1600 0`; `zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1603 1 1100 -60 1600 8`; then three pulses: `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1603 20`, wait 10 ticks, `zpwg8 md 1100 -60 1600`, `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1603 0`, wait 10, `md`. Type, dye, wrench: `zpwg8 mdtype 1100 -60 1600 0 5`; `zpwg8 hold minecraft:red_dye`; `zpwg8 use 1100 -60 1600 north 0.25 0.75 0.0`; `zpwg8 hold create:wrench`; `zpwg8 use 1100 -60 1600 north 0.25 0.75 0.0`; `md`. Value box (empty hand on the slot centre, not sneaking): `zpwg8 hold minecraft:air`; `zpwg8 use 1100 -60 1600 north 0.25 0.75 0.0`; `md`. Removal: `zpwg8 sneak on`; `zpwg8 use 1100 -60 1600 north 0.75 0.75 0.0`; `md`; `zpwg8 sneak off`. Burnout, Z 1606: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1606 powergrid:modular_display facing=north`; `zpwg8 fp 1100 -60 1604`; `zpwg8 hold powergrid:display_module 1`; `zpwg8 use 1100 -60 1606 north 0.25 0.75 0.0`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1609 0`, wired T0 and T8 as above; `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1609 40`; `md 1100 -60 1606` after 2, 10 and 40 ticks; `cdevtest items 1100 -60 1606 3`. Drops: `setblock 1100 -60 1600 minecraft:air destroy`; `cdevtest items 1100 -60 1600 2`
@pass insert: both `use` lines `result=SUCCESS` or `CONSUME`, `held after` 3 then 2, `md slot 0 module=zerotonine:0:false:white`, slot 1 the same, slots 2 and 3 `empty`; pulses: after each 20 V step `index` +1 with `halfClick=true` (`zerotonine:1:true:white`), after each 0 V step `halfClick=false`, ending at `zerotonine:3:false:white` (20 V over the 25 ohm coil = 0.8 A, above 0.5 A; 16 W, under 25 W); `mdtype`: slot 0 `alphabet:0:false:white:0` (color kept); dye: slot 0 `alphabet:0:false:red:0` (the click reached the block: no value box cancel; port change, PORT_NOTES.md section 19), `held after=minecraft:red_dyex1` (not consumed, upstream-same); wrench: `blankingRemoved=1`; value box: nothing changes (Create's handler takes the click on the slot center; on a client it opens the module type board; record `result`); removal: slot 1 `empty`, `held after=powergrid:display_modulex1`; burnout: 40 V gives 1.6 A, 64 W: `temp` rises past 125 within 10 ticks, then slot 0 `empty` and `temp=22` (module burnt; no drop: `drops 0`, upstream-same); drops of the first display: `drop powergrid:modular_display x1` and `drop powergrid:display_module x1` (slot 0 left; slot 1 removed); no ERROR
@fails no insert: `ModularDisplayBlock.use` (face and slot from the hit point); index never moves: `ModularDisplayBlockEntity.electricalTick` (coil switch states `defaultSlotWires`), wiring to T8; dye or wrench do nothing: `CustomValueBoxTransformer.testHit` and `ForgeEvents.recordInteractingItem` (the server side needs the recorded item; Create's `ValueSettingsInputHandler` at NORMAL priority); never burns: `ThermalBehaviour.shouldOverheat` (`overheating` config), `DisplaySlotThermal.tick`
