## SQ-PWG-64 | PWG-38 CRT electron gun (anode current by grid and heater), encasing with andesite and brass, dye, sneak-wrench back
@group A
@commands PWG-38 (CRT), Z 1615. `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1615 powergrid:crt facing=north`. Heater (T1) to cathode (T0): `zpwg3 src 1103 -60 1615 12`; `zpwg3 w 1103 -60 1615 0 1100 -60 1615 1`; `zpwg3 w 1103 -60 1615 1 1100 -60 1615 0`. Anode (T3) through a current gauge: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1619 powergrid:current_gauge facing=north`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1622 1000`; `zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1622 0 1100 -60 1619 0`; `zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1619 1 1100 -60 1615 3`; `zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1622 1 1100 -60 1615 0`. Grid (T2): `zpwg3 src 1097 -60 1615 0`; `zpwg3 w 1097 -60 1615 0 1100 -60 1615 2`; `zpwg3 w 1097 -60 1615 1 1100 -60 1615 0`. Wait 40 ticks, then after each change (wait 40): `zpwg8 crt 1100 -60 1615`, `zpwg3 be 1100 -60 1619`; changes: grid `zpwg3 src 1097 -60 1615 -5`, then `-10`, then `0`; heater `zpwg3 src 1103 -60 1615 8`, then `13`. Encasing, Z 1625: `zpwg3 place 1106 -60 1625 powergrid:crt facing=north`; `zpwg8 fp 1106 -60 1623`; `zpwg8 hold create:andesite_casing`; `zpwg8 use 1106 -60 1625 up 0.5 0.6875 0.5`; `zpwg8 hold minecraft:lime_dye`; `zpwg8 use 1106 -60 1625 north 0.5 0.5 0.0`; `zpwg8 crt 1106 -60 1625`; `zpwg8 hold create:wrench`; `zpwg8 sneak on`; `zpwg8 use 1106 -60 1625 north 0.5 0.5 0.0`; `zpwg8 sneak off`; `zpwg8 crt 1106 -60 1625`; `zpwg8 hold create:brass_casing`; `zpwg8 use 1106 -60 1625 up 0.5 0.6875 0.5`; `crt` again
@pass electron gun (current gauge value, the anode current): heater 12 V (1 A), grid 0: about 0.1 A (1000 V / (10 x 0.01 x 1) = 10 kohm); grid -5 V: about 0.05 A; grid -10 V: about 0 (cut off); grid 0, heater 8 V (0.67 A, below the 0.8 A minimum): about 0; heater 13 V (1.08 A): about 0.117 A; `crt terminals` T1 - T0 = the heater voltage, T3 - T0 about 1000 minus the gauge drop; encasing: block after `powergrid:andesite_encased_crt[facing=north]`; dye: `color=5` (lime) on the encased CRT; sneak wrench: back to `powergrid:crt[facing=north]` (record whether the casing comes back: upstream sets the block only); brass casing: `powergrid:brass_encased_crt` with `color=14` (red: every case change replaces the block entity, so the color resets; upstream-same; the sneak-wrench step also reads `color=14`); no ERROR
@fails current never flows: `CRTBlockEntity.electricalTick` / `tick` (anode-cathode resistance from the grid and heater current), terminal order (`CRTBlock.TERMINALS`: cathode 0, heater 1, grid 2, anode 3, X coil 4, Y coil 5, coil common 6); no encasing: `CRTBlock.use` -> `tryEncase`, `EncasingRegistry.addVariantTo(CRT)` in `ModdedBlocks`
