## SQ-PWG-66 | PWG-40 CC: Tweaked peripherals (probe side and a real computer, B17 main-thread setValue), display link to a display board
@group A
@commands PWG-40, Z 1660. Probe side: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1660 powergrid:voltage_gauge facing=north`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1657 12`; `zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1657 0 1100 -60 1660 0`; `zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1657 1 1100 -60 1660 1`; wait 40; `zpwg8 periph 1100 -60 1660`; `zpwg8 periph 1100 -60 1619` (SQ-PWG-64's current gauge, if still wired); `zpwg3 place 1101 -59 1660 powergrid:redstone_converter facing=north`; `zpwg8 periph 1101 -59 1660`; `zpwg8 conv 1101 -59 1660 7`; wait 20; `zpwg3 be 1101 -59 1660`; `zpwg8 conv 1101 -59 1660 clear`; wait 20; `zpwg3 be 1101 -59 1660`. Real computer: `mkdir -p OUT/srv/<level-name>/computercraft/computer/7 && cp tools/scratch_query/pwg_p8_cc_startup.lua OUT/srv/<level-name>/computercraft/computer/7/startup.lua`; `setblock 1101 -60 1660 computercraft:computer_advanced{ComputerId:7,On:1b}` (its west neighbour is the gauge, the converter is above it); wait 200 ticks, `zpwg3 be 1101 -59 1660` (inside the program's 10 s setValue window); wait 300 more; `cat OUT/srv/<level-name>/computercraft/computer/7/pwg_out.txt`. Display link: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1666 create:display_board facing=north`; power the board from its X side first (Create 0.5.1 skips a board at speed 0): `zpwg3 place 1098 -60 1666 create:creative_motor facing=east`; `zpwg3 place 1099 -60 1666 create:shaft axis=x`; `zpwg3 scroll 1098 -60 1666 32`; `zpwg3 place 1100 -59 1660 create:display_link facing=up`; wait 20; `zpwg8 dlink 1100 -59 1660 1100 -60 1666 2`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1657 -5`, wait 40, `zpwg8 dlink 1100 -59 1660 1100 -60 1666 2`
@pass `periph type=powergrid_voltage_gauge voltage=` about 12 = `getValue`, `maxRange` the gauge range, `rangePercentage` = 12 / range; current gauge `type=powergrid_current_gauge current=` the SQ-PWG-64 gauge value; converter `type=powergrid_redstone_converter`; `conv override=7` then `override=null`, and the converter's terminal voltage follows (record both readings); computer file: `start`, three `sample N peripherals=2` blocks, each with a `powergrid_voltage_gauge` line (`voltage=` about 12, the same as `periph`) and a `powergrid_redstone_converter` line; `top setValue(7) ok=true` and `top clearValue ok=true` (fix B17: main-thread calls; record the side names), `end`; the `be` inside the window shows the 7 override's voltage; display board text (`board ... nbt=`) contains the gauge value with its unit (about `12 V`, then about `-5 V` in polarized mode 2); no ERROR, no CC `LuaException` in the file or the log
@fails no file: the computer did not start (`On:1b`; CC: Tweaked server config `computer_threads`; check `computercraft/computer/7/` exists) or the program errored (CC writes nothing to the server log: rerun by hand in CQ-PWG-21); `peripherals=0`: `CCBridge` provider not registered (SQ-PWG-62 log) or the block entity type does not match (`ModdedBlockEntities.VOLTAGE_METER`); `setValue` error: B17 `mainThread` change; board empty: `activeTarget=none` (the board must be its own controller: wait longer after placing), board speed 0 (motor and shaft on its X side; `DisplayBoardTarget` skips an unpowered board), the display source (`ModdedDisplaySources.ELECTRIC_GAUGE`, P2)
