## CQ-PWG-19
@group client
@commands P8 client boot with the `-10` jar (client mods plus the jar; never `mods/` of the instance), single-player superflat world with cheats, creative: creative tab (Plotter, Alarm Bell, Cathode Ray Tube, Punch Card Reader, Modular Display, Display Module, Punch Card, Incomplete Punch Card; no encased CRT entries); place each block. CRT: creative voltage sources heater 12 V (T1-T0), anode 1000 V (T3-T0), X coil (T4-T6) and Y coil (T5-T6) each an AC source of 15 V amplitude, 0.5 Hz, the Y one a quarter period later (or two DC sources changed by hand); look at the screen (screenshot `RES/shots/CQ-PWG-19_crt.png`); dye it blue; encase with andesite then brass casing, sneak-wrench back; grid -3.5 V. Plotter: creative motor 64 RPM, AC source 10 V amplitude on a 20 V range; screenshot; hover the paper with goggles. Punch card: right-click a card in the air: the screen opens; punch about 10 holes (click), rename it, press accept; reopen (holes and name kept); sign it (tooltip on the sign button), reopen (locked, author line); hover the card (author tooltip). Put the card into a reader driven at 32 RPM (card moves through). Modular display: insert modules, hold right-click on a slot (module type board), choose Alphabet; wrench-hover a slot (overlay text); pulse the slot 0 coil with a source toggled 0 / 20 V; drive 40 V on slot 1 (burnout). Alarm bell: 10 V source, then 0. All with `/flywheel backend off` and back on for the plotter and reader shafts
@pass client reaches a world; no `Mixin apply failed`; LOOK: every P8 block and item has its model (no purple/black), the encased CRTs show their casing; CRT: a glowing dot or Lissajous trace in the screen (additive render type), the trace color follows the dye, the grid voltage dims it; plotter: the paper scrolls, the pointer swings with the voltage, a graph line is drawn on the paper in the dye color, the goggles show the time header and value and three outline lines on the paper; punch card screen: background, 16 x 8 hole buttons with hover and punched states, paper bits fly when punching, the name field edits (typing `e` does not close the screen), accept closes, the data and name persist (`SaveCardC2SPacket`), after signing the author and name are drawn as text (port: no StringWidget) and the buttons are locked; reader: the card model slides through; modular display: the module digits render in the slots (sprite strips), the board lists `0 - 9`, `9 - 0`, `1 - 0`, `Hexadecimal`, `Symbols`, `Alphabet` (not `create.` keys: port change), the wrench overlay reads `Blanking page: Enabled` / `Disabled`, flips click, the burnt slot throws sparks and a burst sound and empties; bell: rings while powered and plays its end sound when cut; shafts turn in both Flywheel modes, none doubled or missing; no `Error`, `Exception` or `Missing model` naming `powergrid` in the client log
@fails missing model: shipped `models/block/plotter/*`, `punch_card_reader/*`, `crt_background`, `modular_display/block` and the `ModdedPartialModels` P8 entries; no CRT trace: `CRTRenderer` (`ModdedRenderLayers.getAdditiveCrt`), client config `crtPointCount`; graph or paper scroll missing: `PlotterRenderer` (`PAPER_SHIFT`: Create 0.5.1 `SpriteShifter`, the `plotter_paper_shift` texture must be stitched); screen issues: `PunchCardScreen`, `PunchCardButton` (`renderButton`); module digits missing: `ModularDisplayBlockEntityRenderer` (`RenderType.text` on `textures/block/modular_display/*`); raw keys on the board: `ModularDisplayBlockEntity` option board override
