## CQ-PWG-21
@group client
@commands PWG-38 to -40 by hand on a dedicated server (the `-10` jar on both sides; CC: Tweaked on both): an advanced computer next to a voltage gauge on a 12 V source and a redstone converter; in the computer `lua`: `peripheral.getNames()`, `peripheral.call("<side>", "voltage")`, `peripheral.call("<side>", "setValue", 9)` then `clearValue`; edit a punch card (holes, name, sign) and drop it, pick it up again; insert it into a reader by hand and by hopper; modular display: insert a module, dye the slot by clicking its centre with a dye, toggle the blanking page with a wrench on the centre, hold right-click with an empty hand (board) and pick Symbols; burn a slot out at 40 V while standing next to it; alarm bell on and off
@pass `getNames` lists both sides; `voltage` returns about 12 (matches the gauge and its goggle line); `setValue` returns without error and the converter output follows, `clearValue` restores it (B17); the card keeps its holes, name and lock across drop and pickup (server-side `SaveCardC2SPacket`, `Locked`, `Author`); the reader takes it both ways; on the display the dye and wrench work on the slot center (port: server-side held-item check), the board sets Symbols; the burnout shows sparks and sound on the client with no client log error (B16: queued on the client thread); the bell sound starts and stops; no exception in either log
@fails dye or wrench ignored on the server only: `ForgeEvents.recordInteractingItem` (registered on the forge bus with the other `ForgeEvents` handlers); CC call errors: the peripheral class named in the error; burnout error in the client log: `DisplayBurnoutS2CPacket.handle`
