## SQ-PWG-06 | 2026-11-14 row: board convergence (diode to regulator unchanged), thyratron rewritten: grid -30 before heater and anode; fire at 0, latch at -30, anode break resets
@group A
@commands Non-linear convergence (moved here from the performance section; values from the offline harness, BoardComponentTests). Diode, Z 1710: `zpwg9 board 1100 -60 1710 diode`; `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1714 powergrid:creative_resistor`; `zpwg3 res 1100 -60 1714 54`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1713 5`; `zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1713 0 1100 -60 1714 0`; `zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1714 1 1100 -60 1710 0`; `zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1713 1 1100 -60 1710 1`; `zpwg9 watch 1100 -60 1710 100`; after the watch `zpwg3 be 1100 -60 1714`, `zpwg9 bcomp 1100 -60 1710`; then `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1713 -5`, `watch` 100, `bcomp`. NPN, Z 1720: `zpwg9 board 1100 -60 1720 npn`; Rc `zpwg3 place 1098 -60 1724 powergrid:creative_resistor`, `res ... 54`; Rb `zpwg3 place 1102 -60 1724 powergrid:creative_resistor`, `res ... 72`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1727 5`; wires: src T0 to Rc T0 and to Rb T0, Rc T1 to board T0 (collector), Rb T1 to board T1 (base), board T2 (emitter) to src T1; `watch 1100 -60 1720 100`; `zpwg9 bcomp 1100 -60 1720`; `zpwg3 be` on both resistors; saturation: `zpwg3 res 1102 -60 1724 58` (5 k), `watch` 100, `bcomp`. PNP, Z 1730: `zpwg9 board 1100 -60 1730 pnp` with the same three blocks at Z 1734 / 1737 but wired emitter side up: src T0 to board T0 (emitter), board T1 (base) to Rb T0, Rb T1 to src T1, board T2 (collector) to Rc T0, Rc T1 to src T1; Rb 100 k then 5 k as for the NPN. Triode, Z 1740: `zpwg9 board 1100 -60 1740 triode`; heater `zpwg3 src 1103 -60 1740 6`, wires to board T3 and T4; anode `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1747 250`, `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1744 powergrid:creative_resistor`, `res ... 63` (10 k), src T0 to resistor T0, resistor T1 to board T0, src T1 to board T2; grid `zpwg3 src 1097 -60 1740 0`, T0 to board T1, T1 to board T2; `watch 1100 -60 1740 200` (heater warm-up); `zpwg3 be 1100 -60 1744`; `bcomp`; then grid `zpwg3 src 1097 -60 1740 -4`, `watch` 100, `be`; heater off `zpwg3 src 1103 -60 1740 0`, `watch` 200, `be`. Pentode, Z 1750: `zpwg9 board 1100 -60 1750 pentode`, wired as the triode at Z 1750 plus the screen: `zpwg3 src 1106 -60 1750 150`, T0 to board T5, T1 to board T2; grid 0 then -4 as above. Regulator tube, Z 1760: `zpwg9 board 1100 -60 1760 regulator`; `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1764 powergrid:creative_resistor`, `res ... 58` (5 k); `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1767 150`; src T0 to resistor T0, resistor T1 to board T0, board T1 to src T1; `watch 1100 -60 1760 100`; `zpwg9 bcomp 1100 -60 1760`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1767 200`, `watch` 100, `bcomp`. Thyratron, Z 1770 (rewritten 2026-11-14, plan_bugfix_1114.md 8.3 `#84`: upstream's thyratron latches once struck while the anode current holds, so the grid goes to -30 V **before** heater and anode come up): `zpwg9 board 1100 -60 1770 thyratron`; grid first: `zpwg3 src 1097 -60 1770 -30`, T0 to board T0, T1 to board T1; heater `zpwg3 src 1101 -60 1771 6.5` with short wires to board T2 and T3 (6.5 V as the pwg12 batch; one block: the heater is 150 W, about 25 A; if a wire burns, record it and use `powergrid:golden_wire` as the 10th `w` argument); `watch 1100 -60 1770 200` (heater warm-up, anode not yet wired); anode `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1777 0`, `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1774 powergrid:creative_resistor`, `res ... 54` (1 k), src T0 to resistor T0, resistor T1 to board T4 (top cap), src T1 to board T1 (cathode); `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1777 200`; `watch` 100; `bcomp`; grid `zpwg3 src 1097 -60 1770 0`, `watch` 100, `bcomp`; latch: grid back `zpwg3 src 1097 -60 1770 -30`, `watch` 100, `bcomp`; break the anode current `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1777 0`, `watch` 40, then `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1777 200`, `watch` 100, `bcomp`
@pass every `watch end` has `firstConverged` between 1 and 5 and a `settledAt` (not -1) under 40, except the triode and pentode heater warm-up (record the tick; settled within the 200); diode: forward drop T0 - T1 0.55 to 0.75 V (harness 0.617 V at 4.38 mA; the junction warms a little), resistor current (5 - drop) / 1 k; reverse: T0 - T1 about -5 V, resistor current under 0.01 mA; NPN 100 k: Vbe (T1 - T2) 0.4 to 0.8 V (harness 0.474), Vce (T0 - T2) about 4.1 V, Rc current about 0.91 mA, Rb current about 45 uA, ratio 18 to 22 (gain 20); 5 k: Vce under 0.4 V; PNP the same with signs mirrored; triode: grid 0 V, anode current (10 k drop / 10 k) about 14.4 mA (harness 14.36 mA, Va 106 V) once the heater is warm; grid -4 V: about 13.0 mA (harness 13.05 mA, Va 119.5 V), `settledAt` up to about 35 ticks (B18: `firstConverged` comes earlier, record both); heater off: the current falls to about 0 within the 200 ticks; pentode: about 21.5 mA at grid 0 and 17.7 mA at -4; regulator: T0 - T1 about 60.7 V from 150 V and 61.1 V from 200 V (it strikes above 84 V and holds); thyratron: grid -30 V with the anode brought up after it: no conduction (T4 - T1 near 200 V minus the leak); grid 0 V: it fires and T4 - T1 holds near 12 V (record); grid back to -30 V: still conducting (latched, as upstream `ThyratronWire`); anode current broken and restored at -30 V: no conduction again; no NaN in any line, no `Solution possibly not converged` warning spam (one or two after a step are fine; with `logsEnabled` false none print)
@fails `settledAt=-1` or values that keep moving: the step limits `triodeLim*` / `diodeLimAlpha` (`CSolver`), record the series of terminal values; diode drop far off: the board diode model (`DiodeComponent.bake`, PNJunctionWire temperature callback); tubes never conduct: the heater wiring (T3 / T4) or the thermal callback (`setSaturationCurrent`), record `bcomp` thermal
