## SQ-PWG-69 | board parts with state: redstone relay (south input), switch used twice, capacitor charging through 10 k
@group A
@commands Board parts with state, Z 1780. Redstone relay: `zpwg9 board 1100 -60 1780 relay_rs`; `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1786 powergrid:current_gauge facing=north`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1783 10`; src T0 to gauge T0, gauge T1 to board T0, board T1 to src T1 (as SQ-PWG-68); wait 20; `zpwg3 be 1100 -60 1786`; `setblock 1100 -60 1781 minecraft:redstone_block` (south of the board: the relay's input side); wait 10; `be`; `zpwg9 bcomp 1100 -60 1780`; `setblock 1100 -60 1781 minecraft:air`; wait 10; `be`. Switch: `zpwg9 board 1106 -60 1780 switch`, wired the same with its own gauge and source at X 1106; wait 20; `be` on its gauge; `zpwg9 fp 1106 -60 1778`; `zpwg9 buse 1106 -60 1780 5 6`; wait 10; `be`; `buse` again; `be`. Capacitor: `zpwg9 board 1112 -60 1780 capacitor`; `zpwg3 place 1112 -60 1786 powergrid:creative_resistor`, `res ... 63` (10 k: RC = 1 s with 100 uF); `zpwg3 src 1112 -60 1783 0`; src T0 to resistor T0, resistor T1 to board T0, board T1 to src T1; `zpwg3 src 1112 -60 1783 10`; then `zpwg9 bmap 1112 -60 1780` after 0, 20, 40 and 100 ticks
@pass relay: open (no redstone): gauge about 0; with the redstone block: about 0.1 A and `bcomp` `redstone_relay@5,6 ... props[redstone_relay_powered=true ...]`; after removing it: about 0 again; switch: about 0 first (`switch_state=false`), `buse ... result=SUCCESS` (or CONSUME), about 0.1 A after the first use, about 0 after the second; capacitor: T0 - T1 rises from 0 toward 10 V: about 6.3 V after 20 ticks (one RC, backward Euler gives about 6.2), about 8.6 at 40, about 10 at 100
@fails relay never closes: the input side (`CircuitBoardBlock.getOrientation`, the relay's orientation DOWN takes the south neighbor on a flat north-facing board; try the other three sides and record which works), `neighborChanged`; switch: `SwitchComponent.use` / `tick`; capacitor jumps: `CapacitorComponent` charge property
