## SQ-PWG-70 | board as an item: pick-block copy, plain board removes itself, drops, overheat and repair, creative sneak repair, fan cooling
@group A
@commands Board as an item, damage and cooling, Z 1790. Copy: `zpwg9 board 1100 -60 1790 triode`; `zpwg9 pick 1100 -60 1790`; `zpwg9 fp 1104 -60 1788`; `zpwg9 pick 1100 -60 1790` (into the fake player's hand); `zpwg9 use 1104 -61 1790 up 0.5 1.0 0.5`; `zpwg9 bmap 1104 -60 1790`. Plain board: `zpwg9 hold powergrid:circuit_board`; `zpwg9 use 1106 -61 1790 up 0.5 1.0 0.5`; `execute if block 1106 -60 1790 powergrid:circuit_board`. Drops: `setblock 1100 -60 1790 minecraft:air destroy`; `zpwg9 drops 1100 -60 1790 2`. Overheat: `zpwg9 board 1110 -60 1790 resistor`; `zpwg3 src 1110 -60 1793 100`; src T0 to board T0, src T1 to board T1; `zpwg9 bcomp 1110 -60 1790` every 10 ticks for 60 ticks; `zpwg3 src 1110 -60 1793 0`; `zpwg9 repair 1110 -60 1790`; `bcomp`; then the creative action: `zpwg3 src 1110 -60 1793 100`, wait 60, `zpwg3 src 1110 -60 1793 0`, `zpwg9 fp 1110 -60 1788`, `zpwg9 mode creative`, `zpwg9 sneak on`, `zpwg9 hold minecraft:air`, `zpwg9 use 1110 -60 1790 up 0.5 0.125 0.5`, `bcomp`. Cooling: `zpwg9 board 1120 -60 1790 resistor`; `zpwg3 place 1118 -60 1790 create:encased_fan facing=east` (blowing at the board at 1120; if it blows the other way use `facing=west`); `zpwg3 place 1117 -60 1790 create:creative_motor facing=east`; `zpwg3 scroll 1117 -60 1790 256`; wait 40; `zpwg9 bcomp 1120 -60 1790`; `setblock 1117 -60 1790 minecraft:air`; wait 40; `bcomp`
@pass copy: `pick powergrid:circuit_board Schematic=true components=6`, `use ... result=SUCCESS` (or CONSUME), the new board's bundles equal the first one's (the same 5 terminals); plain board: `use` places it and it removes itself (upstream: a board without a schematic has no circuit), `execute if block` fails, no drop; drops: `drop powergrid:circuit_board x1 Schematic components=6 Thermal`; overheat: the resistor unit climbs past 175 and stops at 185 (the cap, overheat 175 + 10; was 125 / 135 before jar -17, run r1114) within about 40 ticks, then the circuit opens (T0 - T1 = 100 V, no further heating; on a client the part shows burnt and sparks: CQ-PWG-22); `repair` cools nothing but rebakes: `thermal` back at ambient, the circuit conducts again; the creative sneak use does the same (`use ... result=SUCCESS`); cooling: `cooling=` above 1 while the fan runs (1 + the fan's factor), back to 1 after the motor is removed
@fails copy without schematic: `CircuitBoardBlock.getCloneItemStack`; the placed copy is empty: `setPlacedBy` (`CircuitSchematic.fromStack`); drop without tags: the loot table `copy_nbt` (shipped `loot_tables/blocks/circuit_board.json`); never overheats: `ThermalBehaviour.shouldOverheat` (`overheating` config); cooling stays 1: the P9a branch of `AirCurrentMixin` (`addCoolingMultiplier`)
