## CQ-PWG-22
@group client
@commands P9a client boot with the `-12` jar (client mods plus the jar; never `mods/` of the instance) joining a dedicated scratch server set up as SQ-PWG-67 (probes in the server only); creative tab (Pins, Relay, Double Pole Relay, Resistor, Redstone Relay, Diode, Static Induction Transistor, NPN BJT, PNP BJT, Capacitor, Potentiometer, Triode, Pentode, Thyratron, Regulator Tube, Barretter Tube, Varistor; no Circuit Board, no Incomplete ... entries); `grep -n 'component items' logs/latest.log` (client); in game: `/zpwg9 board X Y Z NAME` near the player for `resistor`, `diode`, `npn`, `triode` (powered as SQ-PWG-06, heater on), `relay_rs`, `switch`, `capacitor`, and `/zpwg9 ponder ...` for `resistor` and `thyratron`; screenshot each (`RES/shots/CQ-PWG-22_<name>.png`); overheat a resistor board (SQ-PWG-70) while watching; `reload` on the server and grep the client log again; ponder: `/create ponder powergrid:resistor`, `powergrid:triode`, `powergrid:potentiometer`, `powergrid:display_module`, `create:copper_nugget` (via), `create:encased_fan`, and the Circuit Components tag page; screenshot at 3 s and at the end
@pass client log `Received 28 component items from the server` at join and again after `reload`; boards render: the plate, the copper traces and pads (not purple-black: the two sprites come from the board model's `getMaterials`, since `atlases/blocks.json` does not ship), each part's model at its place and turn (diode facing left, relay arrow down), the triode's heater glow when warm, the redstone relay's on state; the overheated resistor turns dark with sparks and a crackle; the board's terminals show as wire connection points; ponder: every scene opens (no `Could not find`), boards in the scenes show their parts and traces, the circuits run (gauges move, tubes glow, the display module flips); the tag page lists the 26 members; no exception with `org.patryk3211.powergrid` or `circuits` in the client log
@fails purple traces: `UnbakedCircuitBoardModel.getMaterials`; no part models: `ModelEvent.RegisterAdditional` (`ComponentModels.collectRawIds`), the loader name `circuit_board`; no sync line: `PowerGridImpl.datapackSync`; ponder board empty: the structure's `Schematic` read on the client (`CircuitBoardBlockEntity.read`)
