## CQ-PWG-23
@group client
@commands By hand on CQ-PWG-22's server: right-click the switch part of a powered `switch` board (`/zpwg9 board`); the potentiometer: `/place template pwgponder:circuit/potentiometer ~2 ~ ~2` (the SQ-PWG-67 ponder datapack), wire its board's two outer terminals to a 10 V source (`/zpwg9 bmap` names them) and hold right-click on the knob; creative, empty hands, sneak right-click a burnt board; multimeter on a trace of a powered resistor board and on a terminal; debug item on a part; Jade / WTHIT and goggles on a board
@pass the switch flips with a click sound and the gauge follows; the potentiometer opens the value board (Create's) after holding right-click for 3 ticks and the set value changes the divider (port: `CustomValueSettingsScreen` on Create 0.5.1's screen); sneak-use repairs the board (parts back to normal); the multimeter takes a trace point and reads its voltage; the debug item prints `Component wires:` with the part's wires in chat; goggles show the board's lines; no client log exception
@fails click does nothing: `CircuitBoardBlock.use` hit test (`IInteractableComponent.getShape`, the board's rotation); potentiometer: `CustomValueSettingsScreen.clientTick` (`PowerGridClient.clientTick`), `UpdateComponentBiPacket`
