@@text `CircuitBoardBlock.use`, which opens the board edit menu for a creative player with empty hands). It adds the `circuit_design_table` block (block entity, glow renderer; 480 ohm, powered from
@@text 30 W, so 120 V across its cord socket; creative players ignore power), the `circuit_schematic` item, the editor
@@text screens, 4 menus (`circuit_design_table`, `_edit`, `_load`, `circuit_board_edit`; 7 in all), 2 packets (`CHANGE_SCREEN`,
@@text `SAVE_SCHEMATIC`, appended after `COMPONENT_ITEMS`) and the JEI ghost drag onto the editor. No new recipe (94): the
@@text table's crafting recipe waits for `copper_plating` (P10) and `deploying/schematic_copy` for P9c; rows use `/give`. Fixes
@@text B21 (both packets now need a loaded block within 8 blocks), B22 (board editor name kept), B23 (a write waits for an empty
@@text output slot), B24 (editor right-click removals and option changes count as unsaved changes). New probe
@@text `tools/scratch_query/pwg_p9b_probe.js` (`zz_pwg_p9b_probe.js`, `zpwg9b`, commands in its header; fake player
@@text `[zpwg9b]`; its `fromboard`, `write`, `load`, `screen`, `bedit` encode and decode the real packet and run its server side
@@text as the fake player, so they test what an editor sends). Area: X 1090 to 1130, Z 1805 to 1850, Y -60
@@text (`forceload add 1090 1805 1130 1850`). Table slots: 0 load, 1 save (blank), 2 output. On a dedicated server the empty
@@text design's name prints as the key `item.powergrid.circuit_schematic.empty` (server-side lang).
@@text
@@text **Run order (high priority first):** SQ-PWG-72 (boot, registries, menus, packets, recipes), CQ-PWG-24 (client: open
@@text the table and the editor, every tool, save; the GUI port is the main crash risk), SQ-PWG-73 (table power by cord, the
@@text two packets with B21 / B23, schematic item NBT round trip, write and load), SQ-PWG-74 (a design saved on the table
@@text becomes a board that solves), SQ-PWG-75 (board edit menu and board editor save, creative only, B22), CQ-PWG-25 (client:
@@text board editor, JEI drag, load screen files, B24 by hand).
@@text
@@table
## SQ-PWG-72 | rerun of the P9b check on -17: zpwg9 check (SQ-PWG-67 tag), zpwg9b check, reload (version, phase, counts: SQ-PWG-90)
@group A
