## SQ-PWG-73 | rerun: design table power by cord (100 / 130 V) with step lines, menus, packets, B21 reach with the menu closed, item NBT round trip, write (B23) and load
@group A
@commands PWG-41 (P9b part: the table and its packets), Z 1810. Power: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1810 powergrid:circuit_design_table facing=north`; `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1813 powergrid:socket facing=down`; `zpwg3 src 1103 -60 1813 100`; `zpwg3 w 1103 -60 1813 0 1100 -60 1813 0`; `zpwg3 w 1103 -60 1813 1 1100 -60 1813 1`; `zpwg9b cord 1100 -60 1813 1100 -60 1810`; wait 20; `zpwg9b tbe 1100 -60 1810`; `zpwg3 src 1103 -60 1813 130`; wait 20; `zpwg9b tbe 1100 -60 1810`; `zpwg9b menus 1100 -60 1810`. Packets: `zpwg9 board 1106 -60 1810 resistor`; `zpwg9b fp 1100 -60 1812`; `zpwg9b fromboard 1100 -60 1810 1106 -60 1810 Test Resistor`; `zpwg9b itemrt 1100 -60 1810`; `zpwg9b screen 1100 -60 1810 1`; `zpwg9b screen 1100 -60 1810 2`; `zpwg9b screen 1100 -60 1810 0`. Reach (B21): `zpwg9b fp 1100 -60 1825`; `zpwg9b fromboard 1100 -60 1810 1106 -60 1810 Far Name`; `zpwg9b screen 1100 -60 1810 1`; `zpwg9b fp 1100 -60 1812`. Write and load: `zpwg9b slot 1100 -60 1810 1 create:empty_schematic`; `zpwg9b write 1100 -60 1810`; `zpwg9b slot 1100 -60 1810 1 create:empty_schematic`; `zpwg9b write 1100 -60 1810` (B23: output still full); `zpwg9b move 1100 -60 1810 2 0`; `zpwg9b load 1100 -60 1810`
@pass `cord socket ... result=true/true` (or a cord-next message) and `cord table ... result=true/true`, `cord entities near:` lists a cord entity; at 100 V `isPowered=false power=` about 20.8, state `powered=false` light 0; at 130 V `isPowered=true power=` about 35, state `powered=true`, light 7; `menus`: `menu 0 powergrid:circuit_design_table class=CircuitDesignTableMenu slots=39`, `menu 1 powergrid:circuit_design_table_edit ... slots=36`, `menu 2 powergrid:circuit_design_table_load ... slots=0`; `fromboard packet bytes=` a few hundred, `fromboard applied menu=powergrid:circuit_design_table`, table `before: schematic name=null components=0 after: schematic name="Test Resistor" components=3`; `itemrt ... Schematic components=3 name="Test Resistor" ... safeNbtEqual=true`; `screen 1 applied menu=powergrid:circuit_design_table_edit`, `screen 2 ... _load`, `screen 0 ... circuit_design_table`; far: `fromboard ... after:` still `name="Test Resistor" components=3` (not "Far Name") and `screen 1 applied menu=inventory`; first write: `slot 1 empty`, `slot 2 powergrid:circuit_schematic x1 Schematic components=3 name="Test Resistor"`, table `components=0 name=null`; second write: slot 1 keeps `create:empty_schematic x1`, slot 2 unchanged; load: slot 0 keeps the schematic (slot 1 is not empty), table `name="Test Resistor" components=3`; no ERROR with `powergrid`
@fails cord fails: the hit points (socket box `SOCKET_DOWN` top at 3 px, the table's back socket at z 14 px), or power the table some other way and record (the packets do not need power); `apply threw`: send the error line (a fake player menu open on the dummy connection); far packet applied: B21 check in `SaveSchematicC2SPacket.apply` / `ChangeScreenC2SPacket.apply`; second write replaced slot 2: B23 check in `CircuitDesignTableBlockEntity.writeToItem`; `safeNbtEqual=false`: `CircuitSchematic.toItemStack` / `fromStack`
