@commands PWG-41 (a design saved on the table becomes a board that solves), Z 1820, after SQ-PWG-73 (the table holds "Test Resistor", slot 0 its schematic, slot 1 a blank). `zpwg9b write 1100 -60 1810`; `zpwg9b toboard 1100 -60 1810 1106 -60 1820`; `zpwg9 bmap 1106 -60 1820`; `zpwg3 place 1106 -60 1826 powergrid:current_gauge facing=north`; `zpwg3 src 1106 -60 1823 10`; `zpwg3 w 1106 -60 1823 0 1106 -60 1826 0`; `zpwg3 w 1106 -60 1826 1 1106 -60 1820 0`; `zpwg3 w 1106 -60 1823 1 1106 -60 1820 1`; wait 20; `zpwg3 be 1106 -60 1826`; `zpwg9 bcomp 1106 -60 1820`; compare with SQ-PWG-73's source board: `zpwg9 bmap 1106 -60 1810`
