## CQ-PWG-26
@group client
@commands P9c client boot with the `-15` jar (client mods plus the jar; never `mods/` of the instance) joining SQ-PWG-76's server (op, creative then survival). Look at SQ-PWG-77's acid pool (1190 -60 1866) from above and from inside (step in, survival, then step out); `/give @s powergrid:acid_bucket`, place and pick it up by hand. JEI: look up `powergrid:incomplete_circuit` (R and U), the Circuit Designing and Circuit Assembly tabs (the design table and the mechanical arm as catalysts; watch the arm animation for 5 s), `powergrid:unetched_circuit` (R: the sequenced assembly and the mixing recipe), `powergrid:battery` (R: the sequenced assembly with the spout step), `powergrid:acid` fluid (R: mixing). Hover an incomplete circuit taken from SQ-PWG-81 halfway (or `/give @s powergrid:incomplete_circuit` with a design: take one from `zpwg9c inc`) and read the tooltip and the item bar. Creative tab: list the new entries. Screenshot each JEI tab (`RES/shots/CQ-PWG-26_<tab>.png`)
@pass the pool renders translucent with the animated acid textures (still and flowing; no purple-black), the fog / overlay inside is plain (no crash), the player takes acid damage with the death message key text on death; the bucket shows its icon, places and picks up acid; JEI: Circuit Designing shows the overlay picture, the Empty Schematic in, the Circuit Schematic out, the circuit components cycling and the design table drawn large; Circuit Assembly shows the overlay, the arm (animated: it swings between the part slot and the depot, the claw holds the cycling component in the middle of the swing), a depot, the Incomplete Circuit and the Circuit Board; the sequenced assemblies show all steps with the transitional items; tooltip: "Circuit Assembly", "Progress: k/3", "Insert <part>" in aqua and "-> Insert <part>" in dark aqua, the bar from orange to cyan; creative tab gains Blazing Acid Bucket and Empty Circuit only (no Unetched Circuit, no Incomplete ... entries); no exception with `org.patryk3211.powergrid` in the client log
@fails crash or black area in a JEI tab: `CircuitAssemblyCategory` / `AnimatedMechanicalArm` (Flywheel 0.6 `TransformStack`, Create 0.5.1 `ArmRenderer` transforms; send the first 20 frames); arm drawn in the wrong place or size: record a screenshot (upstream drew on Create 6's GUI element, layout constants unchanged); purple-black fluid: the textures (`block/acid_still`, `block/acid_flow`) were not stitched: `AcidFluidType` client extension (Create 0.5.1 `TintedFluidType`)
