@@text
@@text **P9d update 2026-11-13 (Integrated Circuit and boost; P9 complete):** jar
@@text `jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-16.jar` (sha1 618ed8016949c7be095f2f7b80156c6316a54000; port
@@text phase **9.4**) supersedes `-15` for every row from here on (the P2 to P9c rows stay valid on it, except the expected
@@text values that change with the boost: `zpwg9b check` and `zpwg9c check` now list the P9d items and recipes as present).
@@text It adds the items `integrated_circuit` (the boosting chip, `BoostingChipItem`, custom renderer) and
@@text `incomplete_electrical_gizmo` (transitional), the `powergrid:boost_recipe` serializer (recipe type `create:deploying`),
@@text 6 recipes (106 in all: `mechanical_crafting/integrated_circuit`, `sequenced_assembly/electrical_gizmo`, the four
@@text `deploying/*_boosting`), the `BoostRecipe` branch of `RecipeApplierMixin` (the boosted tool keeps the tag it went in
@@text with), the Electro-Zapper's chip check, and the `PlayerDrillMixin` boost branch with a way to reach it. A boost gives
@@text 30 % of the tool's max durability in boosted uses (drill and saw 75, baton 6, zapper 15); a boosted drill digs at twice
@@text the speed and draws twice the energy, the saw cuts twice as fast for twice the energy, the baton stuns at
@@text (60 - max health) x power (cap 10) for 120 ticks, the zapper shoots at twice the power. Fixes B28 (the chip boosted
@@text whatever the other hand held when its use ended; it now checks the recipe again and is kept without a match) and B29
@@text (the Boosted tooltip line was missing on the baton and zapper). New probe `tools/scratch_query/pwg_p9d_probe.js`
@@text (`zz_pwg_p9d_probe.js`, `zpwg9d`, commands in its header; fake player `[zpwg9d]` for the hand path; `boost`,
@@text `boosted`, `drill0` act on `[zpwg7]`'s main hand). Machines come from `zpwg9c` (`depot`, `deployer`, `line`, `feed`,
@@text `loop`, `show`, `take`). Area: X 1095 to 1200, Z 1920 to 1990, Y -60 (`forceload add 1095 1920 1200 1990`). The
@@text boosted numbers compare against SQ-PWG-58 (drill, saw), SQ-PWG-59 (baton) and SQ-PWG-60 (zapper).
@@text
@@text **Run order (high priority first):** SQ-PWG-84 (boot, registries, mixins, recipes, the `RecipeApplierMixin` unit
@@text check), CQ-PWG-27 (client: chip render and hand use, JEI, tooltips; client crash risk), SQ-PWG-85 (boost recipes by
@@text deployers on a depot and on a belt), SQ-PWG-86 (hand boost, B28, zapper chip check), SQ-PWG-87 (boosted drill and saw
@@text against SQ-PWG-58), SQ-PWG-88 (boosted baton and zapper against SQ-PWG-59 / -60), SQ-PWG-89 (electrical gizmo
@@text assembly).
