## SQ-PWG-86 | boost by hand (BoostingChipItem use / finish, CustomUseEffectsItem), B28 hand swap, the zapper's chip check
@group A
@commands Boost by hand (`BoostingChipItem` use / finish, Create 0.5.1 `CustomUseEffectsItem`), B28, the zapper's chip check, after SQ-PWG-84. `zpwg9d fp 1120 -60 1930`; `zpwg9d hand powergrid:portable_drill`; `zpwg9d hand powergrid:portable_saw`; `zpwg9d hand powergrid:electrobaton`; `zpwg9d hand powergrid:electrozapper`; `zpwg9d hand minecraft:diamond_pickaxe`; `zpwg9d handswap`; `zpwg9d zappass`
@pass each tool: `hands main=powergrid:<tool> x1 Boosted=none ... off=powergrid:integrated_circuit x2 ...`, `use chip result=PASS using=true usedHand=OFF_HAND remaining=32`, `finish main=powergrid:<tool> x1 Boosted=` 75 (drill, saw), 6 (baton), 15 (zapper) `... chips=1 returned=1`; `again`: `use chip result=PASS using=false` (the boosted tool has no recipe; nothing more); diamond pickaxe: `use chip result=PASS using=false` (no recipe: the chip is not used); `handswap`: `swapped main to minecraft:diamond_sword x1 Boosted=none`, `finish main=minecraft:diamond_sword x1 Boosted=none ... chips=2` (B28: the chip is kept, the sword not tagged; upstream gave the sword `Boosted=468` and used the chip); `zappass`: `zappass unboosted use=PASS projectiles 0 -> 0 main=powergrid:electrozapper x1 Boosted=none` (the zapper passes so the chip can be used), `zappass boosted use=SUCCESS projectiles 0 -> 1 main=powergrid:electrozapper x1 Boosted=14 Damage=1/50 ... chips=2` (no battery: power 0, so 1 wear; if the zap packet to the fake player throws, `use=error ...` and `Damage=0/50` with the projectile still there and `Boosted=14`: the fake player's missing connection, as SQ-PWG-60, record it)
@fails `using=false` for a tool: `findRecipe` (see SQ-PWG-84) or `isBoosted`; no `Boosted` after `finish`: `finishUsingItem` (`getUsedItemHand`, the off hand); `chips=1` after `handswap`: B28 regression; `zappass unboosted use=SUCCESS` with a projectile: the chip check in `ElectroZapperItem.use`
@from batches/r1113pwg/pwgr1.qb
> zpwg9d fp 1120 -60 1930
waitlog \[zpwg9d\] done 20
> zpwg9d hand powergrid:portable_drill
> zpwg9d hand powergrid:portable_saw
> zpwg9d hand powergrid:electrobaton
> zpwg9d hand powergrid:electrozapper
> zpwg9d hand minecraft:diamond_pickaxe
> zpwg9d handswap
> zpwg9d zappass
sleep 1
count \[zpwg9d\] hands main=powergrid:\S+ x1 Boosted=none .*off=powergrid:integrated_circuit x2 >= 5
count \[zpwg9d\] use chip result=PASS using=true usedHand=OFF_HAND remaining=32$ == 5
expect \[zpwg9d\] finish main=powergrid:portable_drill x1 Boosted=75 .* chips=1 returned=1$
expect \[zpwg9d\] finish main=powergrid:portable_saw x1 Boosted=75 .* chips=1 returned=1$
expect \[zpwg9d\] finish main=powergrid:electrobaton x1 Boosted=6 .* chips=1 returned=1$
expect \[zpwg9d\] finish main=powergrid:electrozapper x1 Boosted=15 .* chips=1 returned=1$
count \[zpwg9d\] use chip result=PASS using=false$ == 6
expect \[zpwg9d\] swapped main to minecraft:diamond_sword x1 Boosted=none
expect \[zpwg9d\] finish main=minecraft:diamond_sword x1 Boosted=none .* chips=2 
expect \[zpwg9d\] zappass unboosted use=PASS projectiles 0 -> 0 main=powergrid:electrozapper x1 Boosted=none
expect \[zpwg9d\] zappass boosted use=.* projectiles 0 -> 1 main=powergrid:electrozapper x1 Boosted=14 Damage=[01]/50 .*chips=2$
reject \[zpwg9d\] finish error
reject \[zpwg\w*\] (error|unknown subcommand)
reject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(Exception|/ERROR\]).*(powergrid|patryk)
look zappass boosted: use=SUCCESS with Damage=1/50 (no battery: power 0, one wear) or use=error ... with Damage=0/50 (the zap packet to the fake player; record, as SQ-PWG-60); chips=1 after handswap: B28 regression; zappass unboosted use=SUCCESS with a projectile: ElectroZapperItem.use chip check

