## SQ-PWG-89 | rerun: electrical gizmo sequenced assembly, two lines (Z 1985 and 1988; the byproduct chance is 20 %)
@group A
@commands Electrical gizmo sequenced assembly (the deploying step with the Integrated Circuit; the gizmo was P2 with no way to make it until now), Z 1985, after SQ-PWG-84. `zpwg9c line 1102 -60 1985 plain`; wait 10; `zpwg9c lineck 1102 -60 1985` (again after 5 ticks if it flipped the motor); `zpwg9c deployer 1104 -58 1985 powergrid:copper_coil 8`; `zpwg9c deployer 1106 -58 1985 create:electron_tube 8`; `zpwg9c deployer 1108 -58 1985 powergrid:integrated_circuit 8`; `zpwg9c deployer 1110 -58 1985 minecraft:gold_nugget 8`; wait 10; `zpwg9c feed 1102 -60 1985 powergrid:zinc_sheet`; `zpwg9c loop 1102 -60 1985 on`; wait until `loop done` (about 300 ticks); `zpwg9c show 1112 -60 1985`; `zpwg9c show 1104 -58 1985`, `1106`, `1108`, `1110` (same Y and Z)
@pass `loop done powergrid:electrical_gizmo x1 cycles=0` (one loop: the four deployers in one pass; or, at 7 / 5 / 3 / 2 / 3 %: `powergrid:zinc_sheet`, `create:polished_rose_quartz`, `minecraft:gold_nugget`, `create:copper_nugget`, `minecraft:repeater`: feed another zinc sheet and rerun); the end depot holds `powergrid:electrical_gizmo x1`; each deployer used one (`x7`; the Integrated Circuit is used up as a part, not as a boost); no ERROR
