## CQ-PWG-27
@group client
@commands P9d client boot with the `-16` jar (client mods plus the jar; never `mods/` of the instance) joining SQ-PWG-84's server (op, survival). `/give @s powergrid:integrated_circuit 4`, `powergrid:portable_drill`, `powergrid:electrozapper`, `powergrid:electrobaton`, `powergrid:portable_battery` (wear it charged: creative charge from the tab, or `zpwg7`-style NBT `{Charge:20000}`). Hand boost: chip in the main hand, drill in the off hand, hold right-click 2 s, in first person and in third person (F5); then swap (drill in the main hand, chip in the off hand) on a fresh drill. Zapper: zapper in the main hand, chip in the off hand, right-click. Hover the boosted drill, zapper and baton (boost the baton the same way). Mine some stone with the boosted drill and compare with an unboosted one. JEI: `powergrid:integrated_circuit` (R: mechanical crafting; U: Create's Deploying tab with the four boost recipes, and the electrical gizmo assembly), `powergrid:electrical_gizmo` (R: the sequenced assembly with its four steps). Creative tab: list the new entries. Screenshots `RES/shots/CQ-PWG-27_<what>.png` (chip in use first person, JEI Deploying boost page, tooltips)
@pass the chip renders as its flat item in the GUI and in hand (no purple-black, no crash); while in use it tilts towards the screen center in first person (`BoostingChipRenderer`) and plays the boosting sound about every 7 ticks with the eating animation; after 32 ticks (1.6 s) one chip is gone, the item-break particles show, and the tool's tooltip reads "Boosted" in blue italics (drill, saw, and since B29 also baton and zapper); the boosted tool's bar is light blue (0x34a8eb) while the worn battery powers it; zapper with the chip: no shot, the chip's use starts (eating animation), then the zapper is boosted; the boosted drill visibly digs faster; JEI: the four boost recipes on Create's Deploying page (tool in, Integrated Circuit held, the same tool out), the mechanical crafting pattern, the gizmo assembly with the transitional Incomplete Electrical Gizmo; creative tab gains the Integrated Circuit only (no Incomplete Electrical Gizmo); no exception with `org.patryk3211.powergrid` in the client log
@fails crash or purple-black chip: `BoostingChipRenderer` (Create 0.5.1 custom renderer, `CustomRenderedItemModel`); no eating animation or sound: Create 0.5.1 `CustomItemUseEffectsMixin` / `BoostingChipItem.getUseAnimation`; nothing happens with the chip in the main hand: the client's `use` path (`findRecipe` on the client needs the synced recipes: the boost recipes in JEI prove they synced); boost recipes missing in JEI: Create's Deploying category lists recipes of type `create:deploying` only (the serializer is Power Grid's)
@draft no batch holds this row yet
@@text
@@text **P10 update 2026-11-13 (decor; last port phase):** jar
@@text `jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar` (sha1 cbc2ddee37ca4e8f8d844958a9744bc02c148d4a; port
@@text phase **10**) supersedes `-16` for every row from here on (the P2 to P9d rows stay valid on it; counts in `zpwg ns` /
@@text `zpwg3 recipes` rise as in SQ-PWG-90). Every upstream block, item, entity, block entity and recipe is now registered:
@@text copper plating with its slab and stairs (connected textures, stonecutting and crafting), the ceiling tile and its four
@@text attachments (right-click a ceiling tile with a factory light, wire connector, cord junction or solar panel; a wrench
@@text takes the attachment back; ceiling tiles hold a placement helper), the string light cord (item, entity, light blocks
@@text `string_light_block` along a lit cord) and its dye pattern recipe (`powergrid:crafting_special_string_light_cord`). The
@@text last two overrides are met: the circuit design table and the solar panel bearing are craftable (both need copper
@@text plating). Ponder: `ceiling_tile` and `wire/string_lights` (81 scenes, 79 structures) and the tag Ceiling Tile
@@text Attachments (5 tags). Fixes: B30 (a string light cord's rewire left its old four wires in the network: extra load,
@@text still there after the cord was gone), B31 (light blocks left in the world when a cord came back unlit after a reload), B32 (the ceiling lamp lost
@@text its bulb when broken or wrenched), B33 (copper plating slab and stairs were in no mineable tag, so they dropped nothing;
@@text the double slab dropped one), B34 (a cord crafted with no dye got an empty pattern tag and stopped stacking). New probe
@@text `tools/scratch_query/pwg_p10_probe.js` (`zz_pwg_p10_probe.js`, `zpwg10`, commands in its header; fake player
@@text `[zpwg10]`, survival). Area: X 1095 to 1135, Z 1995 to 2085, Y -60 ground (`forceload add 1095 1995 1135 2085`).
@@text String light numbers: the cord puts a filament load of 2 x 4608 / N ohm across each end (N items), so it draws
@@text V^2 x N / 4608 W in all, V^2 / 4608 W per item (3.125 W at 120 V); filament temperature settles at that power / (3.5 /
@@text 1800) K (about 5 ticks time constant), glows from 600 K, lights the air along it above glow 0.75 (about 1293 K, 108 V)
@@text and burns out above 1800 K (127 V). Copper plating has no oxidation or waxing upstream (a plain casing block).
@@text
@@text **Run order (high priority first):** SQ-PWG-90 (boot, registries, recipes, `zpwg10 check` with B33 / B34), CQ-PWG-28
@@text (client: rendering of every P10 block and the cord, placement by hand, tooltips, JEI; client crash risk), SQ-PWG-91
@@text (attachments, placement helper, wrench, drops, B32), SQ-PWG-95 (string lights on the grid with numbers, B30, B31,
@@text burn-out), SQ-PWG-92 (ceiling lamp on the grid), SQ-PWG-93 (ceiling solar against a solar panel), SQ-PWG-94 (ceiling
@@text connector and junction in a circuit), SQ-PWG-96 (deploying recipes by machines; design table and solar bearing
@@text craftable), CQ-PWG-29 (ponder scenes and tag).
@@text
@@table
