## SQ-PWG-93 | ceiling tile solar against a solar panel (single), and a four-tile multiblock in series
@group A
@commands Ceiling tile solar against a solar panel (as SQ-PWG-54), Z 2030 and 2040, after SQ-PWG-90. `time set 6000`; `weather clear`; `gamerule doDaylightCycle false`; ceiling: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 2030 powergrid:ceiling_tile_solar`; `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 2033 powergrid:creative_resistor`; `zpwg3 res 1100 -60 2033 33`; `zpwg3 w 1100 -60 2030 0 1100 -60 2033 0`; `zpwg3 w 1100 -60 2033 1 1100 -60 2030 1`; reference: `zpwg3 place 1104 -60 2030 powergrid:solar_panel facing=down` with its own resistor at 1104 -60 2033 (index 33) wired the same; wait 100; `zpwg10 solar 1100 -60 2030`; `zpwg6 solar 1104 -60 2030`. Multiblock: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 2040 powergrid:ceiling_tile_solar`, the same at 1101, 1102 and 1103; `zpwg10 solarjoin 1100 -60 2040 1101 -60 2040`, then with 1102 and 1103; resistor at 1100 -60 2043 index 38 (30 ohm) wired to 1100 -60 2040 the same; wait 100; `zpwg10 solar 1100 -60 2040`; `zpwg10 solar 1103 -60 2040`; `gamerule doDaylightCycle true`
@pass single: the ceiling solar's terminal voltage and goggle power equal the solar panel's within 1 % (same normal: the ceiling panel faces up, as `facing=down`); `controller=` its own position, `sky=15`; multiblock: `solarjoin ok` three times, `connected=3` on the controller, `controller=` the same position on 1103, the terminal voltage about 4 x the single panel's (a series string, as SQ-PWG-54); no ERROR
@fails 0 V at noon: `sky` below 15 (something above), or the ceiling BE's raycast (`CeilingTileSolarBlockEntity.sunRaycast`); different from the panel: the ceiling copy's NBT / normal (`facing` DOWN, face UP); `connected=0` after joining: `mergeMultiblock` (record)
