## SQ-PWG-95 | rerun: string light cord on the grid: numbers, B31 (stray light blocks), B30 (rewire leaves no old wires), burn-out
@group A
@commands String light cord on the grid (B30, B31, burn-out), Z 2060, after SQ-PWG-90. `zpwg3 src 1100 -58 2060 0`; `zpwg3 place 1108 -58 2060 powergrid:ceiling_tile_junction`; B31 setup first: `setblock 1103 -58 2060 powergrid:string_light_block` and `setblock 1105 -58 2060 powergrid:string_light_block`; `zpwg10 cord 1100 -58 2060 1108 -58 2060 4 red,green,blue`; wait 20; `zpwg10 lights 1100 -58 2060 1108 -58 2060`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -58 2060 100`, wait 60, `lights`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -58 2060 120`, wait 60, `lights`; B30: `zpwg10 rewire 1100 -58 2060 1108 -58 2060`, wait 60, `lights`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -58 2060 0`, wait 60, `lights`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -58 2060 120`, wait 60; `zpwg10 cut 1100 -58 2060 1108 -58 2060`; wait 10; `lights`; burn-out: `zpwg10 cord 1100 -58 2060 1108 -58 2060 4`; `zpwg3 src 1100 -58 2060 130`; wait 100; `lights`; `zpwgg items 1104 -58 2060 6`
@pass `cord added=true items=4 length=8 pattern=red,green,blue`; at 0 V: `cords 1`, `filament=0 glow=0 lit=false`, `pattern=[b02e26 5e7c16 3c44aa]` (each channel may read one lower: float rounding), and `light blocks in box=0` (B31: the two light blocks set before are gone after the cord's first lazy tick; upstream kept them until the cord next lit and went dark); 100 V: `end ... V=100` at both ends, `filament=` about 1116 (2.17 W per item), `glow=` about 0.42, `lit=false`, 0 light blocks; 120 V: `filament=` about 1607 (3.125 W per item), `glow=1 lit=true`, `light blocks in box=7` (X 1101 to 1107, Y -58: points along the straight line every length / 9, the last inside the junction); after `rewire 1`: unchanged (`filament` about 1607, not overheated); 0 V: `filament` near 0, `lit=false`, 0 light blocks; `cut 1`, then `cords 0`, 0 light blocks, and `end 1108 -58 2060 V=0` (B30: the junction is cut off; upstream's rewires left two extra sets of cord and filament wires in the network, so the junction still read 120 V and the source still fed the filament load with no cord there); burn-out at 130 V (3.67 W per item, settles at about 1886 K > 1800): `cords 0` (the cord burnt: overheated, removed within 5 ticks), 0 light blocks, `items` none (a burnt cord drops nothing); no ERROR
@fails `cord create error`: `IWire.isCord` (the `string_light_cord` wire type file in the jar) or the endpoints (`isValid`: two terminals at each end); `filament=0` at 120 V: the cord's pWires (`StringLightCordEntity.makeWire`) or the end voltages (`end ... V=`); light blocks left at 0 V or after `cut`: `setLightBlocks` / B31 (`state` starts true); `V=120` at the junction after `cut`: B30 regression (`dropWire` first in `makeWire`)
