## CQ-PWG-28
@group client
@commands P10 client boot with the `-17` jar (client mods plus the jar; never `mods/` of the instance) joining SQ-PWG-90's server (op; creative for building, survival for the wrench and crafting checks). Build: a 3 x 3 wall of `powergrid:copper_plating` with a row of its slabs (bottom, top, double) and stairs (straight, inner, outer corners) against it; a 4 x 4 ceiling of `powergrid:ceiling_tile` two blocks up (place one, then right-click it with more tiles: the placement helper), then right-click tiles with a factory light, a wire connector, a cord junction and four solar panels side by side; put a light bulb in the lamp; power it (120 V creative source, wires to the lamp's terminals); merge the four ceiling solars with the wrench on their top face; string light cord: crafting grid cord + red, green, blue dye; place the patterned cord from a cord junction on a pillar to the ceiling tile junction (right-click each end, as the copper cord), power the far end through a socket (120 V) or with a 120 V creative source as one end, then 0 V; hover the cord items (plain and patterned); pick-block (middle click) each attachment; wrench each attachment (side face); break the lit lamp with a pickaxe in survival. JEI: `powergrid:copper_plating` (R: deploying; U: stonecutting and crafting of slab and stairs, the design table, the solar panel bearing), `powergrid:string_light_cord` (R: deploying cord + light bulb), `powergrid:ceiling_tile` (R: deploying with an empty cardboard slot, D13). Creative tab: list the P10 entries. Screenshots `RES/shots/CQ-PWG-28_<what>.png` (plating wall, ceiling with attachments lit, lit string lights, tooltips, JEI)
@pass copper plating renders with connected textures across the wall and onto the slabs / stairs on their full faces (`EncasedCTBehaviour`, the `copper_plating_connected` sheet), no purple-black; ceiling tiles are thin plates on the ceiling, the attachments show their models (lamp glow `ceiling_tile_light_light` additive when lit, connector post, junction, solar panel top with connected texture after the merge); the string light cord hangs like a copper cord with small bulbs along it in the dye order (red, green, blue repeating; plain cord: warm white), dim when off, glowing with a soft halo when powered, and the air along it gives light (block light about 5; F3 on a light block's position); tooltips: "Pattern:" with three colored O, the rated 120 V / 3 W lines on both cords; pick-block gives the attachment (factory light, wire connector, cord junction, solar panel); wrench gives it back and leaves a ceiling tile; the broken lamp drops tile, factory light and bulb (B32); JEI pages as listed (the special dye recipe is not in JEI: record); creative tab gains copper plating, slab, stairs, ceiling tile and the string light cord after the copper cord, no attachments or light block; no exception with `org.patryk3211.powergrid` in the client log
@fails crash or purple-black: the models (`models/block/ceiling_tile/*`, plating) or the CT sprite shift (`ModdedPartialModels.COPPER_PLATING`, `CeilingTileSolarBlockCTBehaviour`); no bulbs on the cord: `StringLightCordRenderer.segmentRenderHook` / texture `entity/bulb`; no light along a lit cord: server SQ-PWG-95 (light blocks); no lamp glow: `CeilingTileLampRenderer` (`ModdedPartialModels.CEILING_LIGHT`, additive layer)
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## CQ-PWG-29
@group client
@commands P10 ponder on the CQ-PWG-28 client. Ponder (W) on `powergrid:ceiling_tile` (scene `ceiling_tile`) and on `powergrid:string_light_cord` (scenes `wire/string_lights` and `wire/cord`); the Ceiling Tile Attachments tag page (from the Ponder index); the tag on the factory light, solar panel, wire connector and cord junction scenes. Screenshots `RES/shots/CQ-PWG-29_<scene>.png`
@pass `ceiling_tile`: the tile falls in, three texts ("The Ceiling Tile is a decorative block.", attachments, "supports a variety of attachments"), the factory light right-click turns it into the lamp, the four attachments drop in at the end, no missing block (79 structures ship); `string_lights`: two cord junctions on girders, the cord appears, lights up warm after the source (120 V), then a red / green / blue cord replaces it and lights; both texts match the lang; the Ceiling Tile Attachments tag (icon ceiling tile) lists ceiling tile, factory light, wire connector, cord junction, solar panel; the five scenes upstream tags with it (connector, cord junction, solar panel x2, factory light x3) show the tag; no exception in the client log
@fails a scene missing: `PowerGridPonderScenes` (structure `ponder/ceiling_tile.nbt`, `wire/string_lights.nbt` in the jar); a dark cord in the scene: `StringLightCordEntity.tick` ponder branch (`PonderLevels.isPonder`); tag empty: `PowerGridPonderTags`
