## SQ-PWG-97 | B37 wire connector support: light connector on a block side (control, break, drops, gauge), heavy connector on top
@group A
@commands Wire connector support (B37; was B35, TODO `#78`), Z 2100. Light connector on a block side: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 2100 minecraft:stone`; `zpwg3 place 1101 -60 2100 powergrid:wire_connector facing=west` (FACING points at the support); `zpwg3 src 1104 -60 2100 12`; `zpwg3 place 1104 -60 2103 powergrid:voltage_gauge`; `zpwg3 w 1104 -60 2100 0 1101 -60 2100 0`; `zpwg3 w 1101 -60 2100 0 1104 -60 2103 0`; `zpwg3 w 1104 -60 2100 1 1104 -60 2103 1`; wait 20; `zpwg3 be 1104 -60 2103`; control (a neighbour change that is not the support): `zpwg3 place 1101 -59 2100 minecraft:stone`; wait 5; `zpwg3 be 1101 -60 2100`; break the support: `setblock 1100 -60 2100 air`; wait 10; `zpwg3 be 1101 -60 2100`; `zpwg3 count 1101 -60 2100 3 powergrid:wire_connector`; `zpwg3 count 1101 -60 2100 6 powergrid:wire`; `zpwg3 be 1104 -60 2103`. Heavy connector on top of a block, Z 2106: `zpwg3 place 1100 -60 2106 minecraft:stone`; `zpwg3 place 1100 -59 2106 powergrid:heavy_wire_connector facing=down`; `zpwg3 src 1104 -60 2106 12`; `zpwg3 w 1104 -60 2106 0 1100 -59 2106 0`; wait 20; `setblock 1100 -60 2106 air`; wait 10; `zpwg3 be 1100 -59 2106`; `zpwg3 count 1100 -59 2106 3 powergrid:heavy_wire_connector`; `zpwg3 count 1100 -59 2106 6 powergrid:wire`
@pass gauge about 12 V before the break; control: the connector still there after the stone above it; after the support goes: block `minecraft:air` at 1101 -60 2100, `count powergrid:wire_connector 1`, `count powergrid:wire` 1 or more (the two wires' items, record the count; a hand break of the same layout gives the same), gauge about 0 V (its T0 wire went with the connector, the network re-solved); heavy: air, `count powergrid:heavy_wire_connector 1`, wire items 1 or more; no ERROR
@fails connector still in place: B37 not in the jar (`AbstractConnectorBlock.canSurvive` / `updateShape`; needs -18) or `facing` given the wrong way (FACING must point at the support); connector gone but no item: drops off in `updateOrDestroy` (flag 32) or the loot table; wires stay or keep the gauge at 12 V: `ElectricBlock.onRemove` -> `ElectricBehaviour.remove` not reached; connector breaks in the control step: `updateShape` direction check
