## SQ-PWG-80b | RECORD: water first, then redstone, blaze powder, rotten flesh at Z 1894 (which recipe runs)
@group A
@commands **2026-11-15 (D4): an unheated acid recipe (rotten flesh + spider eye in water) was added; SQ-PS15-15 reruns this row and adds the unheated case.** Acid, water first (records the known limit of `#82`), Z 1894, after SQ-PWG-80. `zpwg9c basin 1142 -60 1894`; `zpwg9c bfill 1142 -60 1894 minecraft:water 1000`; wait 5; `zpwg9c put 1142 -60 1894 minecraft:redstone 1`; `zpwg9c put 1142 -60 1894 minecraft:blaze_powder 1`; `zpwg9c put 1142 -60 1894 minecraft:rotten_flesh 1`; wait 200; `zpwg9c show 1142 -60 1894`
@pass RECORD (not a FAIL either way): which recipe ran. Expected: Creative Delight's heated water to salt (`water_salt`, 1000 mB -> 2 salt) takes the water before the items land, so the basin shows salt and the three items left, no acid; if acid formed instead (250 mB, water 750), record it; no ERROR
@fails an ERROR or a basin that never settles: the mixer (`show 1142 -58 1894`) or the burner; the limit itself is a plan decision (plan_bugfix_1114.md 8.3), not a bug
@from batches/r1115/p2_r1.qb
> zpwg9c basin 1142 -60 1894
waitlog \[zpwg9c\] done 20
> zpwg9c bfill 1142 -60 1894 minecraft:water 1000
sleep 0.25
> zpwg9c put 1142 -60 1894 minecraft:redstone 1
> zpwg9c put 1142 -60 1894 minecraft:blaze_powder 1
> zpwg9c put 1142 -60 1894 minecraft:rotten_flesh 1
sleep 10
> zpwg9c show 1142 -60 1894
> zpwg9c show 1142 -58 1894
sleep 1
expect \[zpwg9c\] fill minecraft:water 1000/1000 at 1142 -60 1894
reject \[zpwg\w*\] (error|unknown subcommand)
reject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(Exception|/ERROR\]).*(powergrid|patryk)
look RECORD which recipe ran: salt (water_salt) with the three items left, or acid 250 / water 750; basin settled; mixer speed

## SQ-PWG-54r | solar contraption after a restart: re-attaches on its first tick in a forceloaded chunk
@group A
@commands Solar contraption after a restart (TODO `#87`, matches upstream: re-attachment is not saved, the contraption entity re-attaches on its first tick). After SQ-PWG-54 passed; BX = the X of its bearing (1100, or 1340 when the section ran shifted as in r1114). Read before: `zpwg6 contraptions all BX -60 1510`. Stop the server cleanly, boot it again; `forceload add BX 1500 BX+15 1515` (entity-ticking chunks); wait 100; `zpwg6 contraptions all BX -60 1510`; `zpwg6 solar BX -60 1510`
@pass after the restart: one `controlled ... removed=false ... type=powergrid:solar_panel blocks=2 ... attachedToBearing=true` (the probe prints `controller=none` before and after the restart, r1115; not a criterion), `bearing ... movedContraption=set`, `solar` output non-zero at noon (`time set 6000` if the clock moved); no ERROR
@fails `attachedToBearing=false` after 100 ticks in a forceloaded chunk: the entity is not ticking (check `forceload query`) or `SolarPanelBearingBlockEntity.attach` is not called from the contraption tick (`ControlledContraptionEntity` controller lookup); entity gone: the contraption did not save (`contraptions 0`)
@from batches/r1115/p2_r2.qb
bootexpect Done \(
> forceload add 1380 1500 1395 1515
> time set 6000
> weather clear
sleep 5
> forceload query
> zpwg6 contraptions all 1380 -60 1510
waitlog \[zpwg6\] (bearing|done) 20
sleep 1
> zpwg6 solar 1380 -60 1510
sleep 1
expect \[zpwg6\] controlled id=\d+ .*removed=false.*type=powergrid:solar_panel blocks=2 .*controller=\S+ attachedToBearing=true
expect \[zpwg6\] bearing at 1380 -60 1510 movedContraption=set
expect \[zpwg6\] solar powergrid:solar_panel_bearing
reject \[zpwg\w*\] error
reject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(Exception|/ERROR\]).*(powergrid|patryk)
look solar output non-zero at noon; one controlled entity; record controller= (p2_r1b before the restart: controller=none with attachedToBearing=true)

## CQ-PWG-66
@group client
@commands Display board drive by hand (TODO `#86`; not Power Grid: the `Speed:0.0f` text is Create's own display board tag, the board got no rotation). Creative, on a scratch client with the -18 jar: Power Grid creative voltage source at 24 V wired to an Electric Motor; motor output -> `create:shaft` x2 -> `create:display_board` (2x2) touching the last shaft on its back; Create display link on a source (a nixie or the motor's goggle line) targeting the board; look with goggles at the board
@pass LOOK: the board turns (its goggle line shows a speed, not 0) and shows the linked text; the display link's `Speed` source reads the motor's RPM; with the motor unpowered the board stops
@fails the board shows `Speed:0.0f` or does not turn: the shaft does not reach the board's input (Create 0.5.1 drives the display board through its back face; try a cogwheel or a different side and rewrite this row's hookup); the motor turns but the board does not: Create kinetics, not Power Grid
@draft no batch holds this row yet
